('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_4','prepare','prɪ''pɛr','prɪ''per','[v] 准备， 预备','The prosecution wanted more time to prepare their case.  原告想要有更多的时间来准备诉讼。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_5','crusade','kru''sed','kruː''seɪd','[v] 加入十字军， 投身正义运动; [n] 十字军；斗争，运动',''),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_6','supplant','sə''plænt','sə''plænt','[vt] 取代， 代替','Barker was soon supplanted as party leader.  巴克在党内的领导地位很快就被人取代了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_7','surgeon','''sɝdʒən','''sɜːrdʒən','[n] 外科医师','...a heart surgeon.  …一位心脏外科医生。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_8','abrupt','ə''brʌpt','ə''brʌpt','[adj] 突然的， 意外的； 唐突的， 鲁莽的','an abrupt change of plan  计划的突然改变'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_9','discourage','dɪs''kɝɪdʒ','dɪs''kɜːrɪdʒ','[vt] 使泄气， 使灰心； 阻止， 劝阻','You should not let one failure discourage you.  你不该失败一次就灰心丧气。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_10','predispose','''pridɪ''spoz','ˌpriːdɪ''spouz','[v] 事先影响某人； 易受感染','They take pains to hire people whose personalities predispose them to serve customers well.  他们煞费苦心雇用那些具备把顾客服务好的个性的人。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_11','spontaneous','spɑn''tenɪəs','spɑːn''teɪniəs','[adj] 自发的， 自然产生的； 自然的， 无雕饰的','The crowd gave a spontaneous cheer.  人群自发地欢呼起来。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_12','convection','kən''vɛkʃən','kən''vekʃn','[n] 对流； 传送','...clouds which lift warm, moist air by convection high into the atmosphere.  ...云层通过对流把温暖湿润的空气送到高的大气层中。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_13','wreck','rɛk','rek','[vt] 使失事；破坏; [n] 沉船； 失事','Injury threatened to wreck his sporting career.  伤病可能会毁了他的运动生涯。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_14','twinkling','''twɪŋklɪŋ','''twɪŋklɪŋ','[adj] 闪光的; [n] 瞬间，一眨眼','On a clear night, I could see stars twinkling in the sky.  在晴朗的夜晚，我可以看见星星在天空闪烁。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_15','gloomy','''ɡlumi','''gluːmi','[adj] 忧郁的， 令人沮丧的； 昏暗的， 阴暗的， 阴沉的','The report paints a gloomy picture of the economy.  这篇报告描绘了一幅惨淡的经济现状。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_16','reproach','rɪ''protʃ','rɪ''proutʃ','[v&n] 指责， 斥责， 批评','‘You don’t need me,’ she said quietly, without reproach.  “你不需要我。”她语气平静，没有丝毫责备。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_17','customs','''kʌstəmz','''kʌstəmz','[n] 关税， 进口税； 海关','What right does Customs have to search my car?  海关有什么权力搜查我的车？'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_18','warrant','''wɔrənt','''wɔːrənt','[n] 授权，批准；许可证；委任状，执行令; [vt] 保证， 担保； 使正当','The company issued warrants for 300,000 shares.  那家公司发放了30万股的认股权证。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_19','sake','sek','seɪk','[n] 缘故， 理由； 好处','He moved to the seaside for the sake of his health.  他为了健康而迁居海滨。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_20','conceal','kən''sil','kən''siːl','[vt] 隐蔽； 隐瞒； 覆盖','The shadows concealed her as she crept up to the house.  她借着阴影蹑手蹑脚地走向房子。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_21','solid','''sɑlɪd','''sɑːlɪd','[adj] 固体的；实心的；结实的，稳固的；可靠的；连续的; [n] 固体','The lake was frozen solid .  湖水冻得结结实实。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_22','narrative','''nærətɪv','''nærətɪv','[adj] 叙述性的; [n] 叙述；记叙体，叙述技巧','The novel contains more narrative than dialogue.  这部小说里的叙述比对话多。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_23','coincide',',koɪn''saɪd','ˌkouɪn''saɪd','[vi] 同时发生； 一致， 相符； 重合','When our vacations coincided, we often holidayed together.  我们的假期要是凑巧赶在一起，我们常常会一同去度假。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_24','circular','''sɝkjəlɚ','''sɜːrkjələr','[adj] 圆形的， 环形的； 循环的； 绕行的','a circular table  圆桌'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_25','scratch','skrætʃ','skrætʃ','[vt] 刮擦，划；抓，搔; [n] 划痕； 挠痒','John yawned and scratched his leg.  约翰打了个呵欠，挠了挠腿。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_26','require','rɪ''kwaɪr','rɪ''kwaɪər','[vt] 需要； 要求， 命令','Campbell’s broken leg will probably require surgery.  坎贝尔的一条腿骨折，可能需要手术。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_27','cooperative','ko''ɑpərətɪv','kou''ɑːpərətɪv','[adj] 合作的，协作的；配合的; [n] 合作企业','He was doing his best to be cooperative.  他在尽全力配合。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_28','willow','''wɪlo','''wɪlou','[n] 柳， 柳树； 柳木制品',''),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_29','corporeal','kɔr''pɔrɪəl','kɔːr''pɔːriəl','[adj] 肉体的， 身体的； 物质的； 实体的','corporeal desires  肉欲'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_30','irritable','''ɪrɪtəbl','''ɪrɪtəbl','[adj] 急躁的， 易怒的； 易受刺激的； 过敏的','Jo was tired, irritable, and depressed.  乔疲惫暴躁，而且情绪低落。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_31','triple','''trɪpl','''trɪpl','[v] 增至三倍; [adj] 三部分的； 三方的； 三倍的','The company has tripled in size .  这家公司的规模已扩大了两倍。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_32','temper','''tɛmpɚ','''tempər','[n] 脾气，性情; [vt] 缓和， 调节','That temper of hers will get her into trouble one of these days.  她那种脾气早晚会让她惹麻烦的。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_33','legible','''lɛdʒəbl','''ledʒəbl','[adj] 清楚的； 易读的','Her handwriting was so tiny it was barely legible.  她的字写得这么小，简直都看不清楚。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_34','tickle','''tɪkl','''tɪkl','[v] 发痒；使高兴，逗乐; [n] 痒','Mommy, this blanket tickles.  妈妈，这毛毯扎人。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_35','cardiac','''kɑrdɪæk','''kɑːrdiæk','[adj] 心脏的； 心脏病的','cardiac surgery  心脏手术'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_36','accessible','ək''sɛsəbl','ək''sesəbl','[adj] 易接近的； 可得到的； 可进入的','The island is only accessible by boat.  这个岛只有坐船才能到。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_37','ageism','''edʒ''ɪzəm','''eɪdʒɪzəm','[n] 年龄歧视','The problem of ageism in the workplace often goes unrecognized.  工作场所的年龄歧视问题常被忽视。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_38','cliff','klɪf','klɪf','[n] 悬崖， 峭壁','The car rolled over the edge of a cliff.  汽车翻下了悬崖边。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_39','roll','rol','roul','[v] 滚动，转动；卷，绕；摇摆，摇晃; [n] 卷； 卷形物； 名单， 花名册','His sleeves were rolled above his elbows.  他的袖子卷到了胳膊肘的上面。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_40','notable','''notəbl','''noutəbl','[adj] 值得注意的，明显的；显著的；著名的；重要的; [n] 名人， 要人','Every country in the world signed the treaty, with one notable exception - the United States.  全世界每个国家都签署了那份条约，只有一个国家反其道而行之，就是美国。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_41','concede','kən''sid','kən''siːd','[v] 承认； 让步； 允许','‘That’s the only possible solution.’ ‘Yes, I suppose so,’ Charles conceded.  “那是唯一可行的解决办法。”“对，我想是。”查尔斯承认道。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_42','unparalleled','ʌn''pærəlɛld','ʌn''pærəleld','[adj] 空前的， 无比的','an achievement unparalleled in sporting history  体育史上空前的成就'),
