('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_976','cramp','kræmp','kræmp','[n] 痉挛，抽筋；; [vt] 阻碍， 阻止','Several players were suffering from cramp.  有几名球员抽筋了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_977','academy','ə''kædəmi','ə''kædəmi','[n] 学会， 研究院； 专科院校','the American Academy of Arts and Letters  美国艺术和文学学会'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_978','solitude','''sɑlətud','''sɑːlətjuːd','[n] 孤独， 单独； 独处， 独居； 隐居处','the solitude of her house on the lake  她湖边那所房子的清静'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_979','reward','rɪ''wɔrd','rɪ''wɔːrd','[n] 报答，奖赏，报酬; [vt] 奖赏， 奖励， 给以报酬','The school has a system of rewards and punishments to encourage good behaviour.  学校有奖惩制度以鼓励良好行为。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_980','hockey','''hɑki','''hɑːki','[n] 曲棍球','...a new hockey arena.  …一个新的冰球场。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_981','graze','ɡrez','greɪz','[v] 吃草；放牧；擦伤; [n] 擦伤','fields where they used to graze their sheep  他们过去放羊的田野'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_982','swallow','''swɑlo','''swɑːlou','[v] 吞，咽；吞没，侵吞；轻信，轻易接受；默默忍受；使不流露，抑制; [n] 燕子； 吞， 咽','He swallowed the last of his coffee and asked for the bill.  他喝完最后一口咖啡，要求结账。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_983','perquisite','''pɝkwəzɪt','''pɜːrkwɪzɪt','[n] 津贴， 利益； 特权',''),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_984','hominid','''hɑmɪnɪd','''hɑːmɪnɪd','[adj] 灵长目的; [n] 原始人类；人科动物','Extinct genus of african hominid .  以灭绝的非洲原始人类。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_985','nucleus','''nuklɪəs','''njuːkliəs','[n] (原子)核','Neutrons and protons are bound together in the nucleus of an atom.  在一个原子的核内，中子和质子聚合在一起。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_986','sting','stɪŋ','stɪŋ','[v] 刺，蜇；感觉刺痛; [n] 尾刺； 刺痛','He was stung by a bee.  他被蜜蜂蜇了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_987','juice','dʒus','dʒuːs','[vt] 榨出汁液; [n] 汁， 液','a carton of orange juice  一纸盒橙汁'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_988','haste','hest','heɪst','[v] 赶快， 匆忙; [n] 急忙，急速，匆忙','Spelling mistakes are often just the result of haste.  拼写错误经常是由于匆忙而造成的。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_989','nurture','''nɝtʃɚ','''nɜːrtʃər','[vt] 养育，养护，培养；扶植，支持；滋长，助长; [n] 养育， 培养','plants nurtured in the greenhouse  在温室里培育的植物'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_990','buckle','','''bʌkl','[v] 扣紧； 变形， 弯曲; [n] 皮带扣环','The steel pillars began to buckle.  这些钢柱开始变形了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_991','degenerate','dɪ''dʒɛnəret','dɪ''dʒen(ə)rət','[vi] 退化， 衰退; [adj] 堕落的； 退化的','Inactivity can make your joints stiff, and the bones may begin to degenerate.  不活动会使关节僵硬，骨骼因此可能会开始退化。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_992','destructive','dɪ''strʌktɪv','dɪ''strʌktɪv','[adj] 破坏性的， 毁灭性的','the destructive power of modern weapons  现代武器的破坏力'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_993','monastery','''mɑnəstɛri','''mɑːnəsteri','[n] 男修道院， 寺院','They found an icon in the monastery.  他们在修道院中发现了一个圣像。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_994','devout','dɪ''vaʊt','dɪ''vaut','[adj] 虔敬的； 诚恳的','a devout Catholic  虔诚的天主徒'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_995','censor','''sɛnsɚ','''sensər','[n] 审查员; [vt] 审查， 检查','The report was cleared by the American military censors.  这篇报道被美国军方审查员删掉了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_996','devour','dɪ''vaʊɚ','dɪ''vauər','[vt] 狼吞虎咽地吃， 吞食； 吞没， 吞噬； 如饥似渴地读','The boys devoured their pancakes.  男孩子们狼吞虎咽地把薄煎饼吃了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_997','stir','stɝ','stɜːr','[v] 搅拌；煽动；激发，打动；行动，活动; [n] 搅拌， 搅动； 激动， 震动','Stir the paint to make sure it is smooth.  将油漆搅拌至均匀。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_998','insult','ɪn''sʌlt','ɪn''sʌlt','[vt] 侮辱， 凌辱; [n] 侮辱， 凌辱','Nobody insults my family and gets away with it!  谁也别想侮辱了我的家人之后就这么算了！'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_999','existence','ɪɡ''zɪstəns','ɪg''zɪstəns','[n] 存在， 实在； 生存， 生活','Scientists have many theories about how the universe first came into existence (= started to exist ).  关于宇宙的起源，科学家有多种理论。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1000','craft','kræft','kræft','[v] 手工制作; [n] 手艺，工艺','Each doll is crafted individually by specialists.  每个布娃娃都由专业人员手工制作。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1001','axis','''æksɪs','''æksɪs','[n] 轴； 轴线， 中心线','The Earth rotates on an axis between the north and south poles.  地球绕着南北两极之间的地轴自转。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1002','maze','mez','meɪz','[n] 迷宫；复杂难懂的细节；困惑，迷惘; [vt] 使混乱； 使困惑， 迷惑','We got completely lost in the maze.  我们在迷宫中彻底迷了路。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1003','float','flot','flout','[v] 漂浮， 浮动； 飘动','I looked up at the clouds floating in the sky.  我仰望着天上的浮云。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1004','gaseous','''ɡæsɪəs','''gæʃiəs','[adj] 气体的， 气态的','Freon exists both in liquid and gaseous states.  氟利昂既有液态也有气态。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1005','negligent','''nɛɡlɪdʒənt','''neglɪdʒənt','[adj] 忽略的； 疏忽的； 粗心大意的','Mr Brown was found guilty of negligent driving.  布朗先生被判疏忽驾驶罪。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1006','expressive','ɪk''sprɛsɪv','ɪk''spresɪv','[adj] 有表现力的， 富有表情的； 表示…的， 表现…的','You can train people to be more expressive.  你可以培训人们使其更富于表现力。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1007','conductivity',',kɑndʌk''tɪvəti','ˌkɑːndʌk''tɪvəti','[n] 传导性； 传导率','Operating on the borderline of superconductivity and ordinary conductivity, they produce immense amplification.  它们在超导性和普通导电性的临界线上操作，产生巨大的放大效果。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1008','desolate','''dɛsələt','''des(ə)lət','[adj] 荒凉的， 无人烟的； 不幸的， 忧伤的; [vt] 使感到悲惨， 使感到凄凉； 使荒芜','a desolate landscape  荒凉的景色'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1009','coarse','kɔrs','kɔːrs','[adj] 粗糙的； 粗俗的','a jacket of coarse wool  粗羊毛夹克衫'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1010','evade','ɪ''ved','ɪ''veɪd','[v] 逃避， 回避； 躲开， 避开','I could tell that he was trying to evade the issue.  我看得出他在极力回避这个问题。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1011','associative','ə''soʃɪətɪv','ə''souʃiətɪv','[adj] 联想的； 结合的； 关联的','the brain’s ability to form associative links between different things  大脑通过联想把不同事物联系起来的能力'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1012','exaggerate','ɪɡ''zædʒəret','ɪg''zædʒəreɪt','[v] 夸张， 夸大','I couldn’t sleep for three days – I’m not exaggerating.  我三天没睡觉了——一点不夸张。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1013','cortex','''kɔrtɛks','''kɔːrteks','[n] 皮层， 皮质','...the cerebral cortex.  ...大脑皮层。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1014','imply','ɪm''plai','ɪm''plaɪ','[vt] 意味着， 暗示； 说明， 表明； 使有必要','an implied threat  隐含的威胁'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1015','offset',',ɔf''sɛt','''ɔːfset','[n] 分支；补偿；抵消; [vt] 补偿； 抵消','The multiplier on government spending might in fact be close to zero, as each extra dollar is almost entirely offset by increased private saving.  由于每一额外的一美元几乎完全被增长了的私人储蓄所抵消，政府开支乘数实际上可能接近于零。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1016','backhand','''bæk''hænd','''bækhænd','[n] 反手击球','She practised her backhand.  她练习反拍。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1017','cascade','kæ''sked','kæ''skeɪd','[vi] 倾泻，流注; [n] 小瀑布； 倾泻','Her thick black hair cascaded down below her waist.  她那浓密的黑发瀑布般垂过腰际。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1018','cavity','''kævəti','''kævəti','[n] 腔； 洞， 穴， 窟窿； 龋洞','Put herbs inside the body cavity of the fish.  把香草放进鱼肚里。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1019','sequence','''sikwəns','''siːkwəns','[n] 一系列，一连串；顺序，次序，序列; [vt] 按顺序排列','Be careful to perform the actions in the correct sequence .  注意要按正确的顺序来完成动作。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1020','provision','prə''vɪʒn','prə''vɪʒn','[n] 供应， 供应品； 条款； 准备， 预备','He made provisions for his wife and his children in his will.  在遗嘱里他为妻子和孩子都做好了安排。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1021','recruit','rɪ''krut','rɪ''kruːt','[v] 招募，征募; [n] 新兵； 新成员','Most of the men in the village were recruited that day.  村里的大多数男子在那一天应征入伍。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1022','thrust','θrʌst','θrʌst','[v] 挤；插；戳，刺; [n] 戳， 刺； 要旨； 驱动力','She thrust her way into the crowd.  她挤进了人群。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1023','abolition',',æbə''lɪʃən','ˌæbə''lɪʃn','[n] 废除， 废止； 废奴运动','The abolition of slavery in Brazil and the Caribbean closely followed the pattern of the United States.  巴西和加勒比海地区对奴隶制的废除很大程度上遵循了美国的模式。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1024','sporadic','spə''rædɪk','spə''rædɪk','[adj] 偶发的， 间或出现的， 零星的','There has been sporadic violence downtown.  市中心时有暴力事件发生。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1025','turnout','''tɝnaʊt','''tɜːrnaut','[n] 出席人数； 产量， 产额','I was disappointed by the turn-out for our home match.  我对我们主场比赛的观众到场人数感到失望。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1026','configuration','kən,fɪɡjə''reʃən','kənˌfɪgjə''reɪʃn','[n] 布局， 格局； 结构， 构造， 形状； 配置','...Stonehenge, in southwestern England, an ancient configuration of giant stones.  …史前巨石柱群，位于英国西南部，是一座古代巨石阵列。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1027','scientific',',saɪən''tɪfɪk','ˌsaɪən''tɪfɪk','[adj] 科学的； 细致严谨的','We believe in investing in scientific research.  我们相信科学研究的投资价值。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1028','spherical','''sfɪrɪkəl','''sferɪkl','[adj] 球形的， 球状的','...purple and gold spherical earrings.  ...紫色和金色的球形耳环。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1029','chunk','tʃʌŋk','tʃʌŋk','[n] 厚片， 大块； 相当大的部分； 矮胖的人','ice chunks  大冰块'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1030','asteroid','''æstərɔɪd','''æstərɔɪd','[n] 小行星','Astronomers have detected an asteroid not far from Earth, moving in the same orbit around the Sun.  天文学家在距离地球不远处发现一颗与地球绕日轨道相同的小行星。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1031','commonplace','''kɑmən''ples','''kɑːmənpleɪs','[adj] 普通的， 平凡的; [n] 平凡的事；老生常谈','Car thefts are commonplace in this part of town.  镇上的这个地段盗车案屡见不鲜。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1032','libel','''laɪbl','''laɪbl','[vt] 诽谤; [n] 诽谤； 诽谤性文字','The newspaper which libelled him had already offered compensation.  那家诽谤他的报纸已经提出赔偿。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1033','parameter','pə''ræmɪtɚ','pə''ræmɪtər','[n] 参量， 参数； 界限， 范围','The inquiry has to stay within the parameters laid down by Congress.  调查必须局限于国会设定的范围之内。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1034','extinct','ɪk''stɪŋkt','ɪk''stɪŋkt','[adj] 灭绝的， 不存在的； 不再活跃的','Dinosaurs have been extinct for millions of years.  恐龙已灭绝数千万年了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1035','forerunner','''fɔr''rʌnɚ','''fɔːrʌnər','[n] 先驱者， 开路人； 先兆， 预兆','...a machine which, in some respects, was the forerunner of the modern helicopter.  …一台在某些方面是现代直升飞机的前身的机器。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1036','cubism','''kjubɪzəm','''kjuːbɪzəm','[n] 立体派； 立体主义','By 1918 he had moved away from realism again and was blending fantasy—including abstract flying figures—and cubism in his work.  到1918年，他再次摆脱现实主义，而将幻想画的手法（包括抽象的飞行物）与立体派的风格揉合于他的作品之中。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1037','agonize','''æɡənaɪz','''ægənaɪz','[vi] 苦苦思索； 焦虑不已',''),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1038','percolate','''pɝkəlet','''pɜːrkəleɪt','[v] 过滤；渗入，渗透；逐渐流传，传开; [n] 滤液','These ideas were slow to percolate.  这些观念流传得很慢。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1039','opaque','o''pek','ou''peɪk','[adj] 不透明的， 不透光的； 难懂的， 晦涩的','a shower with an opaque glass door  装有不透明玻璃门的淋浴间'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1040','advantage','əd''væntɪdʒ','əd''væntɪdʒ','[n] 优点；优势，有利条件; [vt] 有益于','Younger workers tend to be at an advantage (=  have an advantage  ) when applying for jobs.  年轻点的工人申请工作时往往处于优势地位。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1041','assistant','ə''sɪstənt','ə''sɪstənt','[adj] 辅助的，助理的；副的; [n] 助手， 助教','...the assistant secretary of defence.  …助理国防部长。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1042','humid','''hjumɪd','''hjuːmɪd','[adj] 湿的， 潮湿的； 湿润的','Tokyo is extremely humid in mid-summer.  仲夏的东京十分潮湿。'),
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO words (book_slug, slug, word, phonetic_us, phonetic_uk, meaning, example) VALUES,
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1043','instead','ɪn''stɛd','ɪn''sted','[adv] 代替， 顶替； 反而， 却','Geoff didn’t study law. Instead, he decided to become an actor.  杰夫没学法律，相反，他决定当演员。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1044','controversy','ˈkɑntrəvɝ​sɪ','''kɑːntrəvɜːrsi','[n] 争论， 辩论','a political controversy  政治争议'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1045','command','kə''mænd','kə''mænd','[n&v] 命令； 指挥， 统率','Shoot when I give the command .  我一下命令就开枪。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1046','compulsory','kəmˈpʌlsərɪ','kəm''pʌlsəri','[adj] 必须做的， 义务的； 强制性的； 必修的','the threat of compulsory redundancies  强制性裁员的威胁'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1047','abortive','ə''bɔrtɪv','ə''bɔːrtɪv','[adj] 落空的， 失败的','an abortive military coup  一场未遂的军事政变'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1048','swarm','swɔrm','swɔːrm','[vi] 云集; [v] 密集， 云集； 成群地飞行; [n] 群，一大群','Photographers were swarming around the princess.  摄影师们一窝蜂地围在公主身边。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1049','anticipate','æn''tɪsə''pet','æn''tɪsɪpeɪt','[v] 预见， 预期； 先于…行动','Sales are better than anticipated.  销量比预期要好。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1050','variable','''vɛrɪəbl','''veriəbl','[adj] 易变的；','Expect variable cloudiness and fog tomorrow.  预计明天多云有雾，天气多变。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1051','temple','''tɛmpl','''templ','[n] 寺庙， 教堂； 太阳穴',''),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1052','slash','slæʃ','slæʃ','[v] 砍；大幅削减; [n] 砍痕， 伤痕； 斜线号','Someone had slashed the tires.  有人把轮胎割破了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1053','fabricate','''fæbrɪket','''fæbrɪkeɪt','[vt] 编造； 制造','The police were accused of fabricating evidence.  警方被控捏造证据。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1054','uproot',',ʌp''rut','ˌʌp''ruːt','[v] 根除； 离开家园','...the trauma of uprooting themselves from their homes.  …他们背井离乡的痛苦经历。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1055','tally','''tæli','''tæli','[v] 吻合; [n] 记录；账','Some of the records held by the accounts departments did not tally.  会计部门的一些账目有出入。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1056','landscape','ˈlændskep','''lændskeɪp','[n] 风景，景色；地貌，地形；风景画; [vt] 美化…的环境','the beauty of the New England landscape  新英格兰风光之美'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1057','exception','ɪk''sɛpʃən','ɪk''sepʃn','[n] 除外， 例外','It’s been cold, but today’s an exception.  天气一直寒冷，但今天是个例外。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1058','prevailing','pri''velɪŋ','prɪ''veɪlɪŋ','[adj] 普遍的； 流行的； 一地常刮的， 盛行的','The prevailing mood of public opinion remained hostile.  公众仍普遍持敌对情绪。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1059','temporary','ˈtempəreri','''tempəreri','[adj] 暂时的， 临时的','temporary pain relief  疼痛的暂时缓解'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1060','habitat','''hæbə''tæt','''hæbɪtæt','[n] 自然环境， 栖息地','watching monkeys in their natural habitat  观察自然生活环境中的猴子'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1061','optimal','''ɑptəml','''ɑːptɪməl','[adj] 最佳的， 最理想的','However, if you want optimal shadow quality and performance, there are some additional things to consider.  不过，如果你想要最佳的阴影质量和性能，有一些其他的事情要考虑。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1062','desperate','''dɛspərət','''despərət','[adj] 绝望的； 不顾死活的， 拼命的； 极度渴望的','I had no money left and was desperate.  我身无分文，已经走投无路了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1063','awful','''ɔfl','''ɔːfl','[adj] 不舒服的； 糟糕的； 可怕的； 非常的','The weather was awful.  天气很糟糕。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1064','urge','ɝdʒ','ɜːrdʒ','[v] 促进，力劝；驱赶，驱策; [n] 强烈的欲望， 冲动','The charity urged quick action.  慈善机构敦促迅速采取行动。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1065','handy','''hændi','''hændi','[adj] 可用的； 易使用的， 便利的； 手巧的','It’s quite a handy little tool.  这件小工具非常有用。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1066','anguish','''æŋɡwɪʃ','''æŋgwɪʃ','[v] 极度痛苦; [n] 极度痛苦','And we know of your anguish.  我们了解你们的痛苦。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1067','refraction','rɪ''frækʃən','rɪ''frækʃn','[n] 折射','The sonobuoy permits recording a refraction profile with only one ship.  声纳浮标允许只以一艘船来记录折射剖面。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1068','visual','''vɪʒʊəl','''vɪʒuəl','[adj] 视觉的','Artists translate their ideas into visual images.  画家把自己的思想转换成视觉画面。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1069','sanctuary','''sæŋktʃuɛri','''sæŋktʃueri','[n] 禁猎区， 动物保护区； 庇护所， 避难所； 圣所， 圣殿','His church became a sanctuary for thousands of people who fled the civil war.  他的教堂成了数千逃避内战的人们的一个避难所。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1070','aerobics','ɛ''robɪks','e''roubɪks','[n] 有氧运动','Yoga has become the new aerobics and some people are getting it out of a book or video.  瑜珈已经成为一种新型有氧运动，有些人从书本或录像中学习瑜珈。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1071','inviting','ɪn''vaɪtɪŋ','ɪn''vaɪtɪŋ','[adj] 动人的， 诱人的； 引人注目的','The log fire looked warm and inviting.  篝火看上去温暖诱人。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1072','instruct','ɪn''strʌkt','ɪn''strʌkt','[vt] 指示； 教授','Eva went straight to the hotel, as instructed (= as she had been told ).  伊娃按照指示径直去了宾馆。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1073','agreeable','ə''ɡriəbl','ə''griːəbl','[adj] 使人愉快的； 欣然同意的','We spent a most agreeable couple of hours.  我们非常愉快地度过了几个小时。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1074','merchant','''mɝtʃənt','''mɜːrtʃənt','[n] 商人','He had a job with an Edinburgh wine merchant.  他在爱丁堡的一个葡萄酒商那里做过事。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1075','community','kəˈmjunətɪ','kə''mjuːnəti','[n] 社会； 社团； 群落； 共同体','The new arts centre will serve the whole community.  这座新的艺术中心将为整个社区服务。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1076','ailment','''elmənt','''eɪlmənt','[n] 小病','minor ailments  小恙'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1077','version','''vɝʒn','''vɜːrʒn','[n] 译文， 译本； 版本','the human version of mad cow disease  疯牛病的人类变体'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1078','charismatic',',kærɪz''mætɪk','ˌkærɪz''mætɪk','[adj] 蒙受神恩的； 有超凡魅力的','Martin Luther King was a very charismatic speaker.  马丁•路德•金是个很有感召力的演说家。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1079','overload',',ovɚ''lod','əʊvə''ləʊd','[vt] 使超载， 使过载； 使超负荷； 给…增加负担; [n] 超载； 超负荷','Be careful not to overload the washing machine.  注意别让洗衣机负荷过重。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1080','bronze','brɑnz','brɑːnz','[adj] 青铜色的; [n] 青铜；青铜色；青铜制品；铜牌','a bronze statuette  小青铜雕像'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1081','staunch','stɔntʃ','stɔːntʃ','[adj] 坚定的， 忠诚的','a staunch conservative  忠实的保守党党员'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1082','selection','sɪ''lɛkʃən','sɪ''lekʃn','[n] 选择， 挑选； 精选； 被挑选出来的人， 精选品； 可供选择的事物','The judges have made their final selection.  评委已经作出最后的评选。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1083','adolescence',',ædə''lɛsns','ˌædə''lesns','[n] 青春','Some young people suddenly become self-conscious and tongue-tied in early adolescence.  一些年青人在青春期早期突然变得害羞结舌。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1084','notch','nɑtʃ','nɑːtʃ','[n] 等级，档次；','Her new book is several notches above anything else she has written.  她的新书比她的其他作品高出了好几个等级。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1085','subculture','''sʌbkʌltʃɚ','''sʌbkʌltʃər','[n] 亚文化行为观念， 次文化','the drug subculture of the inner city  旧城区的吸毒亚文化群'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1086','exhale','ɛks''hel','eks''heɪl','[v] 呼出； 散发','Take a deep breath, then exhale slowly.  深吸一口气，然后慢慢呼出。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1087','appropriate','əˈproprɪət;(for v.) əˈproprɪet','əˈprəʊprɪət;(for v.)əˈprəʊprɪeɪt','[adj] 适当的; [vt] 拨款； 占用， 挪用','The timing of the announcement was particularly appropriate .  通告发布的时机很合适。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1088','least','list','liːst','[adv] 最小； 最少； 微不足道; [adj] 最小的；最少的；最不重要的','The journey would impose extra expense on those least able to afford it.  这次旅行会给那些最负担不起的人增加额外的开支。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1089','utility','ju''tɪləti','juː''tɪləti','[n] 功用， 效用； 公用事业','Does your rent include utilities?  你的房租包括公用事业费吗？'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1090','abrasion','ə''breʒən','ə''breɪʒn','[n] 表面磨损','extra protection against abrasion  防止磨损的额外保护'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1091','symphony','''sɪmfəni','''sɪmfəni','[n] 交响乐， 交响曲； 和谐， 协调','Bruckner’s Fifth Symphony  布鲁克纳的《第五交响曲》'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1092','eloquent','''ɛləkwənt','''eləkwənt','[adj] 雄辩的 ； 动人的','an eloquent appeal for support  极具说服力的求助呼吁'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1093','observatory','əb''zɝvətɔri','əb''zɜːrvətɔːri','[n] 天文台， 天文观测站','They visited the observatory yesterday.  他们昨天参观了天文台。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1094','optimistic',',ɑptɪ''mɪstɪk','ˌɑːptɪ''mɪstɪk','[adj] 乐观的','Andrew took a more optimistic view.  安德鲁抱有更为乐观的想法。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1095','proponent','prə''ponənt','prə''pounənt','[n] 支持者； 倡导者','Halsey was identified as a leading proponent of the values of progressive education.  哈尔西被认为是进步教育价值观的首要支持者。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1096','insolvent','ɪn''sɑlvənt','ɪn''sɑːlvənt','[adj] 财力不足的， 破产的','The company was later declared insolvent (= officially said to be insolvent ).  公司随后被宣布破产。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1097','submarine',',sʌbmə''rin','ˌsʌbmə''riːn','[adj] 水下的， 海底的; [n] 潜水艇','submarine plant life  海生植物'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1098','empiricism','ɛm''pɪrə''sɪzəm','ɪm''pɪrɪsɪzəm','[n] 经验论， 经验主义','A basic principle of empiricism is to insist that all knowledge comes from experience.  坚持一切知识都来自于经验，这是经验论的基本原则。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1099','sleek','slik','sliːk','[adj] 光滑而有光泽的；线条流畅的；时髦的; [vt] 使平整光亮','the sleek lines of the new Mercedes  这款新梅赛德斯汽车的优美外形'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1100','particle','''pɑrtɪkl','''pɑːrtɪkl','[n] 微粒， 颗粒； 【语】小品词','dust particles  尘埃'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1101','musician','mjʊ''zɪʃən','mju''zɪʃn','[n] 音乐家， 乐师','a talented young musician  有天赋的年轻音乐家'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1102','typify','''tɪpɪfaɪ','''tɪpɪfaɪ','[vt] 是…的典范； 成为…的特征','the features which typify a Scottish Highland landscape  苏格兰高地典型的地貌特征'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1103','stagnant','''stægnənt','''stægnənt','[adj] 不景气的； 停滞的； 迟钝的； 因不流动而污浊的','a stagnant pond  死水塘'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1104','perceptive','pɚ''sɛptɪv','pər''septɪv','[adj] 感知的， 知觉的； 有洞察力的， 理解力强的','a perceptive young man  一个观察敏锐的年轻人'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1105','annotation','ˌænəˈteʃən','ˌænə''teɪʃn','[n] 注释， 注解','She retained a number of copies for further annotation.  她为进一步解释保留了好多复印件。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1106','minimize','''mɪnɪmaɪz','''mɪnɪmaɪz','[vt] 将…减到最少， 使最小化； 降低， 贬低','Every effort is being made to minimize civilian casualties.  正在尽最大努力减少平民伤亡。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1107','sweep','swip','swiːp','[v] 打扫；席卷，横扫；挥动，舞动；迅速传播；','Bert swept the path in front of the house.  伯特清扫了屋前的小路。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1108','descend','dɪ''sɛnd','dɪ''send','[v] 遗传； 下降； 起源； 降临， 来临','Our plane started to descend.  我们的飞机开始下降。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1109','mechanics','mə''kænɪks','mə''kænɪks','[n] 机械学， 力学； 技巧， 方法','He has not studied mechanics or engineering.  他没有学习过力学或者工程学。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1110','toed','tod','toud','[adj] 有趾的','They then found the same virus lurking in the genome of the three-toed sloth .  然后他们发现同样的病毒也潜伏在三趾树懒基因组里。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1111','maglev','''mæglɛv','''mæglev','[n] 磁力悬浮火车','The engine for maglev trains is rather in noticeable.  磁悬浮列车的车头是相当值得注意的。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1112','logical','''lɑdʒɪkl','''lɑːdʒɪkl','[adj] 逻辑的； 符合逻辑的， 合理的； 有逻辑头脑的','It’s a logical site for a new supermarket, with the housing development nearby.  附近有住宅区，新的超级市场选址在此是合情合理的。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1113','characterize','''kærəktə''raɪz','''kærəktəraɪz','[vt] 以…为特征； 刻画； 描述','Bright colours characterize his paintings.  明亮的色彩是他绘画作品的特点。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1114','descent','dɪ''sɛnt','dɪ''sent','[n] 血统， 世系； 下降','Passengers must fasten their seat belts prior to descent.  乘客在飞机降落之前必须系好安全带。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1115','stunt','stʌnt','stʌnt','[vt] 阻碍生长；遏制; [n] 特技表演； 噱头； 愚蠢行为','Lack of sunlight will stunt the plant’s growth.  缺乏阳光会阻碍植物的生长。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1116','weird','wɪrd','wɪrd','[adj] 怪异的， 神秘的','A really weird thing happened last night.  昨晚发生了一件非常奇怪的事。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1117','farce','fɑrs','fɑːrs','[n] 笑剧， 滑稽剧； 闹剧','She admitted that the interview had been a complete farce from start to finish.  她承认，采访从头到尾完全是一场闹剧。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1118','ridiculous','rɪ''dɪkjələs','rɪ''dɪkjələs','[adj] 荒唐的， 可笑的','That’s a ridiculous idea!  那主意很荒唐！'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1119','intrusion','ɪn''truʒn','ɪn''truːʒn','[n] 侵扰， 干扰； 侵犯； 侵入， 闯入','the unwelcome intrusion of the press  不受欢迎的新闻界的侵扰'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1120','refute','ri''fjʊt','rɪ''fjuːt','[vt] 反驳， 驳斥','It was the kind of rumour that it is impossible to refute.  这是那种不可能推翻的谣言。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1121','severe','səˈvɪr','sɪ''vɪr','[adj] 严重的； 严厉的； 剧烈的； 严峻的， 艰巨的； 朴素的， 不加装饰的','His injuries were quite severe.  他的伤势很严重。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1122','exemplify','ɪɡ''zɛmplɪfaɪ','ɪg''zemplɪfaɪ','[vt] 是…的典型； 例示， 举例证明','The building exemplifies the style of architecture which was popular at the time.  这栋大楼代表了当时流行的建筑风格。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1123','emerge','ɪ''mɝdʒ','i''mɜːrdʒ','[vi] 显露， 暴露； 出来， 现出','The flowers emerge in the spring.  花儿在春天开放。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1124','lease','lis','liːs','[n] 租约；租期; [vt] 出租','The landlord refused to renew his lease.  房东拒绝和他续签租约。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1125','exploit','ɛksplɔɪt; ɪkˈsplɔɪt','ˈeksplɔɪt;ɪkˈsplɔɪt','[vt] 开发； 利用； 剥削; [n] 英勇行为， 业绩， 功绩','Homeworkers can easily be exploited by employers.  在家工作的人容易被雇主剥削。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1126','eager','''igɚ','''iːgər','[adj] 渴望的， 热切的','He’s a bright kid and eager to learn.  他是个聪明的孩子，热爱学习。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1127','evidence','''ɛvɪdəns','''evɪdəns','[vt] 证明; [n] 证据； 迹象； 根据','The volcano is still active, as evidenced by the recent eruption.  最近的喷发证明，这座火山依然活跃。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1128','republic','rɪ''pʌblɪk','rɪ''pʌblɪk','[n] 共和国； 共和政体','the former Federal Republic of Germany  前德意志联邦共和国'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1129','errand','''ɛrənd','''erənd','[n] 差事， 差使','I seemed to spend my life running errands for people.  我好像一辈子都在为别人跑腿。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1130','flamboyant','flæm''bɔɪənt','flæm''bɔɪənt','[adj] 艳丽的， 绚丽夺目的； 炫耀的','He lifted his arms in a flamboyant gesture .  他抬起胳膊，做了个炫耀的手势。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1131','lethal','''liθl','''liːθl','[adj] 致命的； 破坏性极大的， 极其有害的','They were all drinking lethal amounts of tequila!  他们都在不要命地喝特奎拉酒！'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1132','stun','stʌn','stʌn','[vt] 使昏迷； 使震惊； 使…目瞪口呆， 给以深刻印象','Redfern stunned the crowd with a last-minute goal.  雷德芬在最后一分钟进球，使观众很是震惊。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1133','repetition','''rɛpə''tɪʃən','ˌrepə''tɪʃn','[n] 重复， 反复； 重复的事','Children used to learn by repetition.  过去小孩子是通过背诵来学习的。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1134','sled','slɛd','sled','[v] 乘雪橇， 用雪橇运; [n] 雪橇；摘棉机','We got home and went sledding on the small hill in our back garden.  我们回到家，去后院的小山丘上滑雪橇。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1135','polygamous','pə''lɪgəməs','pə''lɪgəməs','[adj] 一夫多妻的， 一妻多夫的','Less than 1 percent of the men in any Muslim country are polygamous.  任何一个穆斯林国家都有不到1%的男子是有多位妻子的。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1136','suspense','sə''spɛns','sə''spens','[n] 担心， 焦虑； 悬念， 不确定','Come on then, tell me what happened; the suspense is killing me (= I feel very excited or anxious because I do not know what will happen next ) .  快来，告诉我发生了什么事。急死我了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1137','gemstone','''dʒɛm,ston','''dʒemstoun','[n] 经雕琢的宝石','Blue turquoise is valued as a gemstone.  蓝色的绿松石被视为宝石。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1138','narrate','næret','nə''reɪt','[v] 讲述， 叙述','The main character narrates the story.  主人公讲述故事。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1139','spring','sprɪŋ','sprɪŋ','[v] 跳跃；涌现，突然出现；突然提出; [n] 泉； 弹簧， 发条； 春天； 跳， 跃','He sprang to his feet (= stood up suddenly ) and rushed after her.  他腾地站起身，冲过去追她。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1140','autonomy','ɔ''tɑnəmi','ɔː''tɑːnəmi','[n] 自治， 自治权； 自主， 自主权','campaigners who want greater autonomy for Corsica  希望科西嘉有更多自治权的活动家'),
