('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1146','faint','fent','feɪnt','[vi] 昏厥，晕倒; [adj] 模糊的，不清楚的；无力的，虚弱的；眩晕的; [n] 昏厥','Several fans fainted in the blazing heat.  几个球迷在炽热高温下晕过去了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1147','elm','ɛlm','elm','[n] 榆树','It was a good table too, sturdily constructed of elm.  这也是一张好桌子，榆木做的，很结实。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1148','shade','ʃed','ʃeɪd','[n] 阴凉处，遮光物；阴暗；色度；差别; [vt] 遮蔽， 遮光','a plant that needs a lot of shade  喜阴植物'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1149','collide','kə''laɪd','kə''laɪd','[vi] 碰撞， 互撞； 冲突， 抵触','A car and a van collided on the motorway.  一辆汽车和一辆小型货车在高速公路上相撞了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1150','cardinal','''kɑrdɪnl','''kɑːrdɪnl','[adj] 主要的，最重要的; [n] 红衣凤头鸟','Having clean hands is one of the cardinal rules when preparing food.  双手洁净是准备食物时的一项最基本要求。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1151','insist','ɪn''sɪst','ɪn''sɪst','[v] 坚持要求； 坚决主张','Stay for supper – I insist!  留下来吃晚餐——一定的！'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1152','evergreen','''ɛvɚɡrin','''evərgriːn','[adj] 常绿的; [n] 常绿树， 常青树','Plant evergreen shrubs around the end of the month.  大约在月末种植常绿灌木。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1153','staggered','''stæɡɚd','''stægərd','[adj] 交错的， 错开的； 震惊的','I was absolutely staggered when I saw the bill.  看到账单时，我大吃一惊。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1154','volume','''vɑljum','''vɑːljuːm','[n] 体积， 容积， 容量； 音量； 卷， 册； 书','the volume of trade  贸易量'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1155','transact','træn''zækt','træn''zækt','[v] 交易； 执行， 处理','Most deals are transacted over the phone.  大多数生意都是在电话里成交的。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1156','catalyst','''kætəlɪst','''kætəlɪst','[n] 催化剂， 触媒； 促使变化的人','I very much hope that this case will prove to be a catalyst for change.  我非常希望这件事终将成为促成变化的催化剂。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1157','guideline','''ɡaɪdlaɪn','''gaɪdlaɪn','[n] 指导方针，指导原则','This chapter gives you some guidelines to help you in your work.  本章将介绍一些指导性原则，为你的工作提供帮助。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1158','loose','lus','luːs','[adj] 松散的， 宽松的； 不精确的， 不严密的； 不牢固的； 自由的， 散漫的','a loose floorboard  松动的地板'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1159','loathsome','''loθsəm','''louðsəm','[adj] 令人厌恶的， 讨厌的','that loathsome little man  那个讨厌的小男人'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1160','flint','flɪnt','flɪnt','[n] 燧石， 打火石','...a flint arrowhead.  ...一个燧石箭头。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1161','preeminent','pri''ɛmɪnənt','prɪ''emɪnənt','[adj] 卓越的， 杰出的','...some of the preeminent names in baseball.  …棒球史上一些杰出的名字。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1162','indignant','ɪn''dɪɡnənt','ɪn''dɪgnənt','[adj] 愤慨的， 恼怒的','an indignant reply  愤慨的回复'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1163','decimal','''dɛsɪml','''desɪml','[adj] 十进位的，小数的; [n] 小数','changing to a decimal system  改为十进制'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1164','hardly','''hɑrdli','''hɑːrdli','[adv] 几乎不， 简直不； 刚刚， 仅仅','The building work has hardly begun.  施工才刚刚开始。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1165','lasting','''læstɪŋ','''læstɪŋ','[adj] 持久的， 永久的','The reforms will bring lasting benefits.  改革将带来长久的利益。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1166','cynical','''sɪnɪkl','''sɪnɪkl','[adj] 愤世嫉俗的， 冷嘲热讽的','a cynical view of human nature  认为人性本恶的一种观点'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1167','technical','''tɛknɪkl','''teknɪkl','[adj] 技术的， 工艺的； 专业的','Our staff will be available to give you technical support .  有我们的员工向你提供技术支持。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1168','outermost','''aʊtɚ''most','''autərmoust','[adj] 最外面的， 离中心最远的','the outermost stars  最远的恒星'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1169','companion','kəm''pænɪən','kəm''pæniən','[n] 同伴， 共事者','For ten years he had been her constant companion .  十年来他一直陪伴她左右。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1170','culminate','''kʌlmɪnet','''kʌlmɪneɪt','[vi] 达到顶点； 告终； 【天】到中天','They had an argument, which culminated in Tom getting drunk.  他们发生了争论，结果导致汤姆喝醉了酒。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1171','tortuous','''tɔrtʃuəs','''tɔːrtʃuəs','[adj] 折磨人的， 令人痛苦的； 曲折的， 蜿蜒的； 含混不清的， 拐弯抹角的','a tortuous path over the mountains to Kandahar  翻山越岭通往坎大哈的一条蜿蜒小径'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1172','paucity','''pɔ:siti','''pɔːsəti','[n] 极小量， 少量',''),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1173','stretch','strɛtʃ','stretʃ','[v] 延伸， 拉长; [n] 一段路程；延伸','The procession stretched for several miles.  游行队伍延伸了数英里。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1174','strand','strænd','strænd','[n] 股，缕；部分，方面; [vt] 使滞留； 使搁浅','She tried to blow a grey strand of hair from her eyes.  她试图吹开眼前的一缕白发。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1175','accomplish','ə''kɑmplɪʃ','ə''kɑːmplɪʃ','[vt] 达到； 完成； 实现','We have accomplished all we set out to do.  所有计划要做的事情，我们都已完成。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1176','constituent','kən''stɪtʃuənt','kən''stɪtʃuənt','[adj] 有宪法制定或修改权的； 组成的， 构成的; [n] 选民；要素，成分','the EU and its constituent members  欧盟及其成员国'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1177','intentionally','','ɪn''tenʃənli','[adv] 有意地， 故意地','Or you can choose to accelerate your growth and intentionally devour life and all it offers .  或者你可以选择加速你的成长，有意地吞噬生活及生活所赐予你的一切。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1178','irritate','''ɪrɪtet','''ɪrɪteɪt','[vt] 激怒， 使烦躁； 刺激','It really irritates me when he doesn’t help around the house.  家里的事情他一点都不帮忙，真让我恼火。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1179','havoc','''hævək','''hævək','[n] 混乱， 大破坏','policies that would wreak havoc on the country’s economy  会危害该国经济的政策'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1180','responsible','rɪ''spɑnsəbl','rɪ''spɑːnsəbl','[adj] 有责任感的， 负责的； 需负责任的； 责任重大的， 重要的','We are determined to bring the people responsible to justice.  我们决意要将肇事者绳之以法。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1181','vagrant','''veɡrənt','''veɪgrənt','[adj] 漂泊的; [n] 无业游民，流浪者','He lived on the street as a vagrant.  他作为一个流浪者露宿街头。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1182','medal','''mɛdl','''medl','[n] 奖牌， 奖章','She won a gold medal at the last Olympics.  她在上届奥运会上赢得一枚金牌。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1183','linen','''lɪnɪn','''lɪnɪn','[n] 亚麻织品； 亚麻布','a linen jacket  亚麻布夹克'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1184','satellite','''sætəlaɪt','''sætəlaɪt','[n] 卫星； 人造卫星','the launch of a communications and weather satellite  气象通信卫星的发射'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1185','packed','pækt','pækt','[adj] 拥挤的； 压紧的','a packed courtroom  挤满人的法庭'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1186','illuminate','ɪ''lumɪnet','ɪ''lʊːmɪneɪt','[vt] 照亮； 启发， 启迪； 阐明， 说明','A single candle illuminated his face.  一支蜡烛照亮了他的脸。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1187','lizard','''lɪzɚd','''lɪzərd','[n] 蜥蜴','Neither the lizard nor the glass has any secrets.  无论是蜥蜴还是玻璃，都没有任何秘密。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1188','delirium','dɪ''lɪrɪəm','dɪ''lɪriəm','[n] 精神错乱， 神志失常','Before she died she had fits of delirium.  去世前她一阵阵地胡言乱语。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1189','preoccupation','prɪ,ɑkju''peʃən','priˌɑːkju''peɪʃn','[n] 主要考虑因素； 全神贯注','Karouzos''s poetry shows a profound preoccupation with the Orthodox Church.  卡鲁佐斯的诗歌表现出对东正教的深切关注。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1190','vow','vaʊ','vau','[v] 发誓; [n] 誓约','While many models vow to go back to college, few do.  很多模特儿发誓要重返大学，但几乎无人做到。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1191','cipher','''saɪfɚ','''saɪfər','[n] 密码， 暗号','an expert in ciphers  密码专家'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1192','protrude','pro''trud','prou''truːd','[v] 突出， 伸出','...a huge round mass of smooth rock protruding from the water.  …从水中突出来的一块光滑的圆形巨石。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1193','residue','''rɛzɪdu','''rezɪduː','[n] 剩余物， 残余物','The flies leave a sticky residue on crops.  苍蝇在庄稼上留下黏糊糊的分泌物。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1194','noted','''notɪd','''noutɪd','[adj] 著名的','a noted author  著名作家'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1195','frenzy','''frɛnzi','''frenzi','[n] 狂暴， 狂热， 疯狂','Doreen had worked herself into a frenzy .  多琳一阵狂怒。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1196','forum','''fɔrəm','''fɔːrəm','[n] 论坛； 讨论会','Members of the council agreed that was an important forum for discussion.  理事会成员们一致认为那是一个用于讨论的重要论坛。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1197','contempt','kən''tɛmpt','kən''tempt','[n] 轻视， 鄙视， 轻蔑','The public is treated with contempt by broadcasters.  公众受到了节目主持人的轻蔑对待。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1198','horizon','hə''raɪzn','hə''raɪzn','[n] 地平线；','In the distance, the dot of a boat appeared on the horizon.  远处小黑点般的一条小船出现在地平线上。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1199','undertaking','''ʌndɚ''tekɪŋ','ˌʌndər''teɪkɪŋ','[n] 任务， 项目； 事业， 企业； 承诺， 保证','Starting a new business can be a risky undertaking.  创办新企业有时是一件有风险的事情。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1200','figurative','''fɪgərətɪv','''fɪgərətɪv','[adj] 比喻的， 借喻的， 象征的； 形象的','He’s my son, in the figurative sense of the word.  打个比方，他就像是我的儿子。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1201','sweat','swɛt','swet','[v] 出汗; [n] 汗；一身汗','I was sweating a lot despite the air conditioning.  尽管开着空调，我仍是满头大汗。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1202','progressive','prə''ɡrɛsɪv','prə''gresɪv','[adj] 进步的； 逐步的， 渐进的； 【语】进行时的','a progressive administration  进步的政府'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1203','betray','bɪ''tre','bɪ''treɪ','[vt] 出卖， 泄露； 辜负， 对…不忠； 流露情感','He felt that she had betrayed him.  他感觉她背叛了自己。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1204','aloft','ə''lɔft','ə''lɔːft','[adv] 在高处； 在空中','He held the trophy proudly aloft.  他骄傲地把奖杯举向空中。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1205','contributory','kən''trɪbjətɔri','kən''trɪbjətɔːri','[adj] 贡献的； 捐助的； 促进的','Smoking is a contributory factor in lung cancer.  抽烟是导致肺癌的一个因素。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1206','deliberate','dɪ''lɪbərət','dɪ''lɪb(ə)rət','[adj] 故意的， 蓄意的； 审慎的， 深思熟虑的; [v] 深思熟虑','a deliberate attempt to humiliate her  对她的故意羞辱'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1207','swear','swɛr','swer','[v] 诅咒； 宣誓， 发誓','Remember that you have sworn an oath and so must tell the truth.  记住你已经宣过誓了，所以必须讲真话。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1208','atmosphere','''ætməsfɪr','''ætməsfɪr','[n] 大气， 大气层； 空气； 气氛， 氛围','The hotel had a lovely relaxed atmosphere .  那家宾馆的气氛轻松愉快。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1209','decorate','''dɛkəret','''dekəreɪt','[v] 装饰， 布置','Children’s pictures decorated the walls of the classroom.  教室的墙上装点着儿童画。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1210','career','kə''rɪr','kə''rɪr','[n] 生涯， 经历； 职业','a teaching career  教学事业'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1211','slacken','''slækən','''slækən','[v] 松弛， 放松； 减缓， 放慢','The heavy rain showed no signs of slackening off.  大雨没有减弱的迹象。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1212','release','rɪ''lis','rɪ''liːs','[n&vt] 释放； 发布， 公开； 发泄','Police arrested several men, who were later released.  警察逮捕了几个人，后来都释放了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1213','charter','''tʃɑrtɚ','''tʃɑːrtər','[vt] 特许设立，给予特权；包租; [n] 纲领， 宣言； 宪章； 特许状','We chartered a boat to take us to some of the smaller islands.  我们包了一条船带我们到一些较小的岛上去。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1214','abiding','ə''baɪdɪŋ','ə''baɪdɪŋ','[adj] 持久的， 永久的','Phil has a deep and abiding love for his family.  菲尔对家人怀有深厚不渝的爱。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1215','liberate','''lɪbə''ret','''lɪbəreɪt','[vt] 解放； 释放','A few days later, our armies liberated the city.  几天以后，我军解放了这座城市。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1216','moral','''mɔrəl','''mɔːrəl','[adj] 道德的，道义上的；有道德的，品行端正的；精神的','It is easy to have an opinion on a moral issue like the death penalty for murder.  对于判谋杀犯死刑这种涉及伦理道德的问题，有个观点并非难事。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1217','diminution','/ˌdɪmɪˈnuːʃn/','ˌdɪmɪ''nuːʃn','[n] 减少， 缩减','...despite a slight diminution in asset value.  ...尽管资产价值略有减少。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1218','aspire','ə''spaɪr','ə''spaɪər','[v] 有志于； 热望， 向往','...people who aspire to public office.  …志在获得公职的人们。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1219','explode','ɪk''splod','ɪk''sploud','[v] 爆炸； 激增； 冲动， 发怒','The device was thrown at an army patrol but failed to explode.  炸弹投向了陆军巡逻队，但没有爆炸。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1220','outbreak','''aʊtbrek','''autbreɪk','[n] 发作； 爆发','a cholera outbreak  霍乱的爆发'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1221','nap','næp','næp','[n] 小睡， 打盹','an afternoon nap  午睡'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1222','manipulate','mə''nɪpjulet','mə''nɪpjuleɪt','[vt] 操作， 处理； 利用， 操纵','He was one of those men who manipulated people.  他是那种要摆布别人的人。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1223','similar','''sɪməlɚ','''sɪmələr','[adj] 相似的， 类似的','We have similar tastes in music.  我们对音乐的品位相近。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1224','ecological','''ikə''lɑdʒɪkl','ˌiːkə''lɑːdʒɪkl','[adj] 生态的','an ecological disaster  生态灾难'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1225','contradict','''kɑntrə''dɪkt','ˌkɑːntrə''dɪkt','[v] 反驳； 同…矛盾， 相抵触','Deborah opened her mouth to contradict, but closed it again.  黛博拉张口想要反驳，但又把嘴闭上了。'),
