('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1906','vibrant','''vaɪbrənt','''vaɪbrənt','[adj] 振动的； 活泼的， 充满生气的','Hong Kong is a vibrant, fascinating city.  香港是座富有活力的迷人城市。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1907','insanity','ɪn''sænəti','ɪn''sænəti','[n] 精神错乱， 疯狂','The court acquitted Campbell on the grounds of temporary insanity.  法庭以坎贝尔一时精神错乱为由判他无罪释放。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1908','recreation',',rɛkrɪ''eʃən','ˌrekri''eɪʃn','[n] 娱乐， 消遣','His only recreations are drinking beer and watching football.  他唯一的消遣就是喝啤酒和看足球比赛。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_1909','skyscraper','''skaɪ''skrepɚ','''skaɪskreɪpər','[n] 摩天楼','With a few exceptions, the technique for building a skyscraper is similar whether you are in Europe or you are in Singapore.  除了少数特例外，不管是在欧洲还是新加坡，建造一幢摩天楼的技术大体上是相似的。'),
