('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2198','suite','sut; swit','swiːt','[n] 套， 组； 套房','a honeymoon suite  蜜月套房'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2199','overwhelm','ovɚˈhwɛlm','ˌouvər''welm','[vt] 淹没， 漫过； 压倒， 击败， 制服； 使难以忍受； 使应接不暇','Grief overwhelmed me.  我悲痛不已。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2200','morgue','mɔrɡ','mɔːrg','[n] 停尸房， 太平间','Police came and took her gently aside and told her they would try to find the name of the morgue.  警察温和地把她拉到了一边，告诉她他们会尽力寻找存放孩子遗体的太平间的名字。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2201','unprecedented','ʌn''prɛsɪdɛntɪd','ʌn''presɪdentɪd','[adj] 空前的','He took the unprecedented step of stating that the rumours were false.  他史无前例地声明那些谣言实属子虚乌有。'),
