('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2611','layer','''leɪr','''ler','[n] 层， 层次','He pulled off layer upon layer of clothing (= many layers of clothing ).  他把衣服一件件地脱掉。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2612','linguistic','lɪŋ''gwɪstɪk','lɪŋ''gwɪstɪk','[adj] 语言的， 语言学的','a child’s linguistic development  儿童的语言发展'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2613','sanitation',',sænɪ''teʃən','ˌsænɪ''teɪʃn','[n] 卫生； 卫生设施， 卫生设备','Overcrowding and poor sanitation are common problems in prisons.  过度拥挤和卫生状况差是监狱里的普遍问题。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2614','elite','ɪˈliːt','ɪ''liːt','[adj] 卓越的，精锐的; [n] 精英','an elite group of artists  一批出类拔萃的艺术家'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2615','ornament','''ɔrnəmənt','''ɔːnəm(ə)nt','[n] 装饰; [vt] 装饰， 点缀','a shelf covered with books and ornaments  摆满书籍和装饰品的架子'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2616','chubby','''tʃʌbi','''tʃʌbi','[adj] 丰满的， 圆胖的','a chubby six-year-old  一个胖乎乎的六岁孩子'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2617','ivory','''aɪvəri','''aɪvəri','[n] 象牙； 象牙制品； 象牙色， 乳白色','an ivory chess set  一副象牙国际象棋'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2618','anomalous','ə''nɑmələs','ə''nɑːmələs','[adj] 异常的； 不规则的','a highly anomalous situation  极其反常的形势'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2619','deficient','dɪ''fɪʃnt','dɪ''fɪʃnt','[adj] 不足的， 缺乏的； 有缺陷的， 不完善的','Women who are dieting can become iron deficient.  节食的女性有可能缺铁。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2620','henceforth',',hɛns''fɔrθ','ˌhens''fɔːrθ','[adv] 从此以后','multiple sclerosis (henceforth referred to as MS)  多发性硬化（以下称为MS）'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2621','preponderance','prɪ''pɑndərəns','prɪ''pɑːndərəns','[n] 优势','There is a preponderance of female students in the music department.  在音乐系里女学生占大多数。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2622','barrel','''bærəl','''bærəl','[n] 桶','The wine is aged in oak barrels.  这种葡萄酒是用橡木酒桶放陈的。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2623','chain','tʃen','tʃeɪn','[n] 链；; [vt] 用链条拴住； 联号， 连锁店','She had a gold chain around her neck.  她脖子上戴了条金项链。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2624','efficient','ɪ''fɪʃnt','ɪ''fɪʃnt','[adj] 有效的， 有效率的； 有能力的， 能胜任的','a very efficient secretary  效率高的秘书'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2625','unify','''junɪfaɪ','''juːnɪfaɪ','[vt] 统一， 联合','Strong support for the war has unified the nation.  对战争的坚决支持使这个国家团结了起来。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2626','consistent','kən''sɪstənt','kən''sɪstənt','[adj] 一致的； 稳定的； 调和的； 始终如一的','The evidence is not consistent.  证词前后不一致。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2627','reverse','rɪ''vɝs','rɪ''vɜːrs','[v] 反转；彻底转变，颠倒；撤销，废除；交换；; [adj] 相反的','Reverse the paper in the printer.  把打印机中的纸翻过来。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2628','ravage','''rævɪdʒ','''rævɪdʒ','[vt] 毁坏； 抢劫， 掠夺','The country has been ravaged by civil war.  这个国家被内战摧毁了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2629','barren','''bærən','''bærən','[adj] 贫瘠的， 荒芜的； 不结果实的， 不育的','Thousands of years ago the surface was barren desert.  很久很久以前，地面还是一片荒漠。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2630','fungi','ˈfʌnˌdʒaɪ; ˈfʌŋˌgaɪ','''fʌŋgaɪ','[n] [fungus的复数]真菌','Without the fungi, this would be just another sandbar.  如果没有真菌，这里将成为另一个沙洲。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2631','permanent','''pɝmənənt','''pɜːrmənənt','[adj] 持久的， 永久的； 固定不变的','He gave up a permanent job in order to freelance.  他放弃了固定工作，为的是当一名自由职业者。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2632','foster','''fɔstɚ','''fɔːstər','[v] 鼓励，促进，助长；培养，抚育；领养; [adj] 代养的','The bishop helped foster the sense of a community embracing all classes.  主教鼓励一种包容各个阶层的社区精神。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2633','receptacle','rɪ''sɛptəkl','rɪ''septəkl','[n] 容器； 插座','a trash receptacle  垃圾箱'),
