('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2648','playwright','''pleraɪt','''pleɪraɪt','[n] 剧作家','The playwright does something remarkable in this scene, but without any impression of straining after an effect.  剧作家在这场中有许多惊人妙笔，但并不给人留下竭力追求表面效果的印象。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2649','interrupt','''ɪntə''rʌpt','ˌɪntə''rʌpt','[v] 打扰； 中断； 阻碍','Will you stop interrupting me!  别打断我的话！'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2650','beat','bit','biːt','[v] 打拍子，指挥；敲打；打败，胜过；跳动; [adj] 疲惫的; [n] 跳动；节拍，节奏；有规律的敲击','Brazil were beaten 2–1.  巴西队以1比2告负。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2651','feasible','''fizəbl','''fiːzəbl','[adj] 可行的， 行得通的','a feasible solution  可行的解决方法'),
