('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2759','march','mɑrtʃ','mɑːrtʃ','[v] 前进， 进发； 行进， 齐步走； 游行示威; [n] 行进，行军；示威游行；进行曲；进行，进展','An estimated 5,000 people marched through the city to demonstrate against the factory closures.  大约有五千人在市里游行示威，抗议关闭工厂。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2760','blast','blæst','blæst','[v] 爆炸；发出尖响；猛烈抨击; [n] 一阵； 爆炸； 冲击波； 响声','The first shot missed and blasted a hole in the far wall.  第一枪没有打中，在远处墙上射出一个洞。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2761','repel','rɪ''pɛl','rɪ''pel','[v] 击退， 驱逐； 排斥； 抵制， 拒绝； 使反感， 使厌恶','The smell repelled him.  这气味让他反感。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2762','publicize','''pʌblɪsaɪz','''pʌblɪsaɪz','[vt] 宣传， 推广， 宣扬','television’s failure to publicize the unemployment issue  电视未能报道失业问题'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2763','underscore',',ʌndɚ''skɔr','ʌndə''skɔː','[vt] 强调； 在…之下画线; [n] 底线','The Labour Department figures underscore the shaky state of the economic recovery.  劳工部的数字突出显示了经济复苏的不稳定。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2764','seashore','''siʃɔr','''siːʃɔːr','[n] 海岸， 海滨','She takes her inspiration from shells and stones she finds on the seashore.  她从她在海岸边发现的贝壳和石头里获取灵感。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2765','series','''sɪriz','''sɪriːz','[n] 系列， 连续； 连续剧','the series of events that led to the outbreak of war  导致战争爆发的一系列事件'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2766','cultivate','''kʌltɪvet','''kʌltɪveɪt','[vt] 耕种； 培养','We cultivated maize and watermelons.  我们种植玉米和西瓜。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2767','thrive','θraɪv','θraɪv','[vi] 茂盛； 茁壮成长； 兴旺， 繁荣','plants that thrive in tropical rain forests  在热带雨林蓬勃生长的植物'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2768','imaginative','ɪ''mædʒɪnətɪv','ɪ''mædʒɪnətɪv','[adj] 富有想象力的； 创新的','an imaginative use of computer technology  计算机技术的妙用'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2769','treadmill','''trɛdmɪl','''tredmɪl','[n] 踏车； 枯燥乏味的工作','the treadmill of working in the office  单调枯燥的办公室工作'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2770','represent',',rɛprɪ''zɛnt','ˌreprɪ''zent','[vt] 代表； 表现； 描绘； 象征','Mr Kobayashi was chosen to represent the company at the conference.  小林先生被选中代表公司出席会议。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2771','dispatch','dɪ''spætʃ','dɪ''spætʃ','[vt&n] 分派， 派遣； 发送','Goods are normally dispatched within 24 hours.  货物一般在24小时内派送。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2772','corpus','''kɔrpəs','''kɔːrpəs','[n] 文集， 文献， 汇编； 语料库','a corpus of spoken English  英语口语语料库'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2773','inconvenient',',ɪnkən''vinɪənt','ˌɪnkən''viːniənt','[adj] 不便的； 让人不舒服的','Can you come at 10:30? I know it''s inconvenient, but I have to see you.  你能10:30来吗？我知道这不方便，但是我必须要见你。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2774','dramatize','''dræmətaɪz','''dræmətaɪz','[v] 改编成戏剧； 戏剧化， 戏剧性地表现','a novel dramatized for television  被改编成电视剧的小说'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2775','absurd','əbˈsɝ​d','əb''sɜːrd','[adj] 可笑的， 荒唐的','It seems an absurd idea.  这似乎是个荒唐的想法。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2776','prior','''praɪɚ','''praɪər','[adj] 在…前的； 优先的','You do not need any prior knowledge of the subject.  你无需事先具备该方面的知识。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2777','trait','tret','treɪt','[n] 特性， 特点','The study found that some alcoholics had clear personality traits showing up early in childhood.  这项研究发现一些酗酒者早在孩童时就表现出明显的个性特征。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2778','landmark','''lændmɑrk','''lændmɑːrk','[n] 路标， 地标； 〈喻〉里程碑','One of Belfast’s most famous landmarks, the Grosvenor Hall, has been demolished.  贝尔法斯特最著名的地标之一格罗夫纳大厦已被拆毁了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2779','vanish','''vænɪʃ','''vænɪʃ','[vi] 消失； 灭绝','My keys were here a minute ago but now they’ve vanished.  我的钥匙刚刚还在这里，现在却不翼而飞了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2780','vault','vɔlt','vɔːlt','[v] 跳过; [n] 拱顶；金库，保险库；撑杆跳','The robber vaulted over the counter and took $200 in cash.  抢劫犯跃过柜台，抢走了200美元现金。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2781','concave','kɑn''kev','kɑːn''keɪv','[adj] 凹的','a concave lens  凹透镜'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2782','dolphin','''dɑlfɪn','''dɑːlfɪn','[n] 海豚','I like dolphin.  我喜欢海豚。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2783','enactment','ɪ''næktmənt','ɪ''næktmənt','[n] 制订， 颁布； 法律， 法规','We support the call for the enactment of a Bill of Rights.  我们支持《权利法案》制定的呼吁。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2784','planet','''plænɪt','''plænɪt','[n] 行星','The picture shows six of the nine planets in the solar system.  这张图片展示太阳系9个行星中的6个行星。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2785','ornithology',',ɔrnɪ''θɑlədʒi','ˌɔːrnɪ''θɑːlədʒi','[n] 鸟类学','Botany, Entomology Herpetology, mammalogy, and ornithology.  收藏植物学、 虫学、虫学、 乳动物学和鸟类学。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2786','prerequisite',',pri''rɛkwəzɪt','ˌpriː''rekwəzɪt','[adj] 必备的， 作为先决条件的; [n] 先决条件，前提','A person with ambition is the prerequisite to success.  一个人有雄心壮志是成功的先决条件。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2787','count','kaʊnt','kaunt','[v] 数，计算；算入；看做，认为；值得考虑，有重要意义; [n] 计数， 计算； 总数； 罪状','I was amazed at the number of plants - I counted 147.  我对植物的数量之多感到惊讶，我数了有147棵。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2788','creep','krip','kriːp','[vi] 缓慢行进； 爬行； 悄悄地移动','He crept back up the stairs, trying to avoid the ones that creaked.  他蹑手蹑脚地回楼上，尽量避开那些嘎吱作响的梯级。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2789','deciduous','dɪ''sɪdʒuəs','dɪ''sɪdʒuəs','[adj] 落叶的； 非永久的， 短暂的','These Texas maples are far enough south that they peak much later than many other deciduous trees in the United States.  这些德克萨斯州枫树是在足够远的南部，它们的憔悴期迟于美国的许多其他地方的落叶乔木。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2790','scholar','''skɑlɚ','''skɑːlər','[n] 学者； 奖学金获得者','a Shakespearean scholar  研究莎士比亚的学者'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2791','contradictory',',kɑntrə''dɪktəri','ˌkɑːntrə''dɪktəri','[adj] 对立的，矛盾的；反驳的; [n] 对立物； 矛盾因素','Customs officials have made a series of contradictory statements about the equipment.  海关官员们对于这种设备做出了一系列相互矛盾的陈述。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2792','accompany','ə''kʌmpəni','ə''kʌmpəni','[vt] 为…伴奏； 陪伴， 陪同； 伴随， 和…一起发生','Children under 14 must be accompanied by an adult.  14岁以下儿童必须有成人陪同。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2793','immediate','ɪ''midɪət','ɪ''miːdiət','[adj] 即刻的； 当前的； 最接近的； 紧接的， 紧靠的','Our immediate response to the attack was sheer horror.  我们对攻击的第一反应就是非常惊恐。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2794','perspicuous','pə''spikjuəs','ˌpɜːr''spɪkjuəs','[adj] 明白易懂的； 明了的',''),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2795','beneficial',',bɛnɪ''fɪʃl','ˌbenɪ''fɪʃl','[adj] 有益的， 有利的','a drug that has a beneficial effect on the immune system  有益于免疫系统的一种药物'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2796','blame','blem','bleɪm','[vt] 谴责，责备; [n] 过失， 责备； 责任','Don’t blame me – it’s not my fault.  别来怪我——又不是我的错。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2797','confusion','kən''fjʊʒən','kən''fjuːʒn','[n] 困惑； 混乱， 混淆','To avoid confusion, the teams wore different colours.  为了避免混淆，各队穿着不同颜色的服装。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2798','platitude','''plætɪtud','''plætɪtjuːd','[n] 陈词滥调， 老生常谈','His excuse was the platitude ‘boys will be boys.’  他还是那一套理由:“男孩总归是男孩。”'),
