('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2947','discredit','dɪs''krɛdɪt','dɪs''kredɪt','[vt] 使丧失声誉；使怀疑; [n] 名誉丧失','...a secret unit within the company that had been set up to discredit its major rival.  …为破坏其主要竞争对手声誉而设的一个公司内秘密单位。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2948','extraordinary','ɪkˈstrɔrdənerɪ; ɪkˈstrɔrdnˌɛrɪ','ɪk''strɔːrdəneri','[adj] 特别的； 非凡的','a woman of extraordinary beauty  容貌出众的女子'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2949','spawn','spɔn','spɔːn','[v] 产卵；产生，促成; [n] 卵','New technology has spawned new business opportunities.  新技术创造了大量新的商机。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2950','sensory','''sɛnsəri','''sensəri','[adj] 感觉的， 感官的','sensory stimuli such as music  音乐等的感官刺激'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2951','puzzle','''pʌzl','''pʌzl','[n] 难题，谜; [vt] 迷惑， 使困惑','The meaning of the poem has always been a puzzle.  那首诗的含义始终是个谜。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2952','mere','mɪr','mɪr','[adj] 仅仅的， 纯粹的','She lost the election by a mere 20 votes.  她仅仅以20票之差落选。'),
