('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2957','glue','ɡlu','gluː','[vt] 胶合，黏合；紧附于; [n] 胶， 胶水','...a tube of glue.  …一管胶水。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2958','orbital','''ɔrbɪtl','''ɔːrbɪtl','[adj] 轨道的','the Earth’s orbital path  地球的运行轨道'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2959','solder','''sɑdɚ','''sɑːdər','[vt] 焊接; [n] 焊料， 焊锡','Fewer workers are needed to solder circuit boards.  焊接电路板需要较少的工人。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2960','envelop','ɪn''vɛləp','ɪn''veləp','[vt] 包围','the enveloping darkness  笼罩四周的黑暗'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2961','firm','fɝm','fɜːrm','[adj] 结实的； 坚定的， 坚决的; [n] 公司','The sofa cushions are fairly firm.  沙发的坐垫很硬。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2962','reflect','rɪ''flɛkt','rɪ''flekt','[v] 反射， 映现； 显示， 表明； 仔细考虑， 深思','The drop in consumer spending reflects concern about the economy.  消费支出的下降反映出人们对经济的担忧。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2963','adventitious',',ædvɛn''tɪʃəs','ˌædven''tɪʃəs','[adj] 偶然的， 偶发的','The adventitious birth of our fourth child completely changed our plan.  第四个孩子偶然的出生，完全改变了我们的计画。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2964','ongoing','''ɑnɡoɪŋ','''ɑːngouɪŋ','[adj] 正在进行的；不间断的；继续存在的; [n] 前进， 发展','their ongoing search for a new director  他们仍在寻找一个新主任'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2965','outfit','''aʊtfɪt','''autfɪt','[n] 全套装备； 全套服装','She bought a new outfit for the party.  她为了这次派对买了套新衣服。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2966','ignorant','''ɪɡnərənt','''ɪgnərənt','[adj] 无知的， 愚昧的； 无知觉的','an ignorant and uneducated man  不学无术的人'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2967','extort','ɪk''stɔrt','ɪk''stɔːrt','[vt] 勒索， 敲诈， 强夺','Corrupt government officials were extorting money from him.  腐败的政府官员那时正向他勒索钱财。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2968','trample','''træmpl','''træmpl','[v] 踩碎； 践踏， 摧残','Many people were trampled in the panic that followed.  很多人在随后的恐慌中被踩伤。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2969','negligible','''nɛɡlɪdʒəbl','''neglɪdʒəbl','[adj] 可以忽略的， 微不足道的； 无关紧要的','The damage done to his property was negligible.  对他财产造成的损失微不足道。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2970','setback','''sɛtbæk','''setbæk','[n] 挫折， 阻碍； 倒退','The team’s hopes of playing in Europe suffered a setback last night.  球队赴欧洲参加比赛的希望昨晚遇到了阻碍。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2971','spray','spreɪ','spreɪ','[n] 浪花；飞沫；','spray from the waves  海浪溅起的水雾'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2972','distinguish','dɪ''stɪŋɡwɪʃ','dɪ''stɪŋgwɪʃ','[v] 区别， 辨别； 使有别于， 成为…的特征； 看清， 听出； 使杰出， 使著名','The light was too dim for me to distinguish anything clearly.  光线太暗，我什么也看不清。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2973','primordial','praɪ''mɔrdɪəl','praɪ''mɔːrdiəl','[adj] 原始的， 最初的； 基本的','the primordial seas  原始海洋'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2974','husbandry','''hʌzbəndri','''hʌzbəndri','[n] 耕种， 务农， 农牧业','animal husbandry  畜牧业'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2975','haircut','''hɛrkʌt','''herkʌt','[n] 理发','Do you like my new haircut?  你喜欢我的新发型吗？'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2976','decorative','''dɛkəretɪv','''dekəreɪtɪv','[adj] 装饰性的， 做装饰用的','a decorative panel above the door  门楣上的饰板'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2977','pointed','''pɔɪntɪd','''pɔɪntɪd','[adj] 尖的， 尖角的； 尖锐的， 尖刻的','a pointed beard  一把山羊胡'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2978','enthusiastic','ɪn,θuzɪ''æstɪk','ɪnˌθuːzi''æstɪk','[adj] 热情的， 热心的','an enthusiastic supporter of reform  改革的热心支持者'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2979','elongate','ɪ''lɔŋɡet','ɪ''lɔːŋgeɪt','[v] 延长， 伸长','Her legs were elongated by the very high heels which she wore.  她穿的高跟鞋非常高，使她的腿显得长了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2980','symptom','''sɪmptəm','''sɪmptəm','[n] 症状； 征兆','One of the most common symptoms of schizophrenia is hearing imaginary voices.  精神分裂症最常见的症状之一是幻听。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2981','fray','fre','freɪ','[vi] 磨损，磨破；烦躁，恼火; [n] 争斗','The collar had started to fray on Ed’s coat.  埃德外套的领子开始出现了磨损。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2982','thereby',',ðɛr''baɪ','ˌðer''baɪ','[adv] 因此， 从而','Our bodies can sweat, thereby losing heat by evaporation.  我们的身体会流汗，由此能通过蒸发散热。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2983','wield','wild','wiːld','[vt] 支配， 掌权， 行使','He remains chairman, but wields little power at the company.  他还是主席，但在公司内没有什么权力。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2984','disastrous','dɪ''zæstrəs','dɪ''zæstrəs','[adj] 灾难性的','a disastrous first marriage  以失败告终的第一次婚姻'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2985','impulse','''ɪmpʌls','''ɪmpʌls','[n] 冲动， 一时的念头； 刺激， 推动力； 脉冲','The eye converts light signals to nerve impulses.  眼睛把光信号转变成神经冲动。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2986','crystallize','''krɪstə''laɪz','''krɪstəlaɪz','[v] 结晶； 明确','The liquid will crystallize at 50 degrees centigrade.  这种液体在50摄氏度时结晶。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2987','subspecies','sʌb''spiʃiz','sʌb''spiːʃiːz','[n] 亚种','Several other subspecies of gull are found in the region.  几个海鸥的其他亚种在此地区被找到。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2988','shower','''ʃaʊɚ','''ʃauər','[v] 淋浴； 下阵雨； 洒落， 纷纷降落； 抛撒; [n] 阵雨，暴雨；淋浴；一阵，一大批','Mike shaved and showered.  迈克刮了脸，冲了个淋浴。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2989','infectious','ɪn''fɛkʃəs','ɪn''fekʃəs','[adj] 传染性的， 传染病的； 有感染力的','infectious diseases  传染性疾病'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2990','concur','kən''kɝ','kən''kɜːr','[v] 同时发生； 意见一致','Local feeling does not necessarily concur with the press.  当地人的看法不一定和媒体一致。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2991','nevertheless',',nɛvɚðə''lɛs','ˌnevərðə''les','[adv] 然而， 不过','What you said was true. It was, nevertheless, a little unkind.  你说的都是实话，只不过有点刻薄。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2992','prominent','''prɑmɪnənt','''prɑːmɪnənt','[adj] 卓著的， 杰出的； 突起的， 凸出的','a prominent Russian scientist  杰出的俄罗斯科学家'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2993','insulin','''ɪnsəlɪn','''ɪnsəlɪn','[n] 胰岛素','diabetic patients requiring insulin  胰岛素依赖型糖尿病患者'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2994','ironic','aɪ''rɑnɪk','aɪ''rɑːnɪk','[adj] 说反话的， 讽刺的； 出乎意料的','Your car was stolen at the police station! How ironic!  你的车在警察局被偷！真让人哭笑不得！'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2995','fundamental',',fʌndə''mɛntl','ˌfʌndə''mentl','[adj] 基础的，基本的，根本的; [n] 基本原则； 基础','We have to tackle the fundamental cause of the problem.  我们必须解决问题的根本原因。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2996','hieratic','''haɪə''rætɪk','ˌhaɪə''rætɪk','[adj] 僧侣的；',''),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2997','entitle','ɪn''taɪtl','ɪn''taɪtl','[vt] 使…有权； 给题名','a documentary entitled ‘The Price of Perfection’  一部名为《完美的代价》的纪录片'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2998','monotony','mə''nɑtəni','mə''nɑːtəni','[n] 单调， 千篇一律','A night on the town may help to break the monotony of the week.  去城里待一晚也许有助改变一周工作生活的单调。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_2999','outline','''aʊtlaɪn','''autlaɪn','[n] 轮廓； 概要， 大纲; [vt] 描绘； 略述','a research proposal outline  研究计划梗概'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3000','counselor','''kaʊnslɚ','''kaunsələr','[n] 顾问； 律师','The counselor bounced up to denounce discount.  顾问上升蹦跳指责折扣。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3001','fade','fed','feɪd','[v] 褪色； 凋谢； 逐渐消失','Hopes of a peace settlement are beginning to fade.  达成和平协议的希望日渐渺茫。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3002','overdue','''ovɚ''dʊ','ˌouvər''duː','[adj] 过期未付的， 逾期的； 过度的， 过火的； 迟到的， 延误的','an overdue gas bill  逾期未付的煤气账单'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3003','nominal','''nɑmɪnl','''nɑːmɪnl','[adj] 名义上的； 微不足道的','the nominal head of the rebellion  这次叛乱名义上的领导人'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3004','excess','''ɛk''sɛs','ɪk''ses; ek-; ''ekses','[adj] 过量的； 额外的; [n] 过度， 超过','Cut any excess fat from the meat.  将肉中多余的肥肉切掉。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3005','perspective','pɚ''spɛktɪv','pər''spektɪv','[n] 展望； 观点， 看法； 远景； 透视图， 透视法； 前途','the artist’s use of perspective  那位画家对透视法的运用'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3006','galaxy','''ɡæləksi','''gæləksi','[n] 星系； [G-]银河系， 银河； 群英','Astronomers have discovered a distant galaxy.  天文学家们发现了一个遥远的星系。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3007','invade','ɪn''ved','ɪn''veɪd','[v] 侵入， 侵略； 侵扰','The Romans invaded Britain 2,000 years ago.  2,000年前古罗马人入侵了英国。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3008','intervening',',ɪntɚ''vinɪŋ','ˌɪntər''viːnɪŋ','[adj] 介于中间的， 发生于期间的','During those intervening years Bridget had married her husband Robert.  在其间的那些年里，布里奇特与罗伯特结为夫妻。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3009','clump','klʌmp','klʌmp','[v] 聚集， 成群； 以沉重的脚步行走; [n] 丛，簇，束；块，团；群，组','Hair and soap had clumped together in the drain.  头发和肥皂在排水管里结成了团。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3010','thorough','ˈθʌrəʊ; θʌro','''θɜːrou','[adj] 彻底的； 详尽的； 一丝不苟的','The doctor gave him a thorough check-up.  医生给他做了一次全面的体检。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3011','democracy','dɪˈmɑkrəsi','dɪ''mɑːkrəsi','[n] 民主政体， 民主制度； 民主国家； 民主精神','a return to democracy after 16 years of military rule  16年军人统治后民主制度的恢复'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3012','peninsula','pə''nɪnsələ','pə''nɪnsələ','[n] 半岛','the Korean peninsula  朝鲜半岛'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3013','evolve','ɪ''vɑlv','i''vɑːlv','[v] 发展； 进化','Animals have evolved camouflage to protect themselves from predators.  动物进化形成了伪装，以保护自身不被捕食性动物所捕食。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3014','congratulation','kən,ɡrætʃu''leʃən','kənˌgrætʃu''leɪʃn','[n] 祝贺， 道喜','letters of congratulation  祝贺信'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3015','abandon','ə''bændən','ə''bændən','[vt] 离弃，放弃; [n] 放纵， 放任','How could she abandon her own child?  她怎么能抛弃自己的孩子呢？'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3016','extol','ɪk''stol','ɪk''stoul','[vt] 赞美， 颂扬','Now experts are extolling the virtues of the humble potato.  现在专家们在颂扬粗陋的马铃薯的种种好处。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3017','household','''haʊshold','''haushould','[adj] 家庭的，家用的；家喻户晓的; [n] 家庭','household chores  家务杂活'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3018','adverse','ædˈvɚs, ˈædˌvɚs','''ædvɜːrs','[adj] 负面的； 不利的； 逆的','They fear it could have an adverse effect on global financial markets.  他们担心这会对全球金融市场产生不利影响。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3019','bulletin','''bʊlətɪn','''bulətɪn','[n] 新闻简报； 公告， 布告； 简报','...the early morning news bulletin.  …早间新闻快报。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3020','ratio','''reʃɪo','''reɪʃiou','[n] 比， 比率','The adult to child ratio is one to six.  成人与儿童之比是1比6。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3021','junction','''dʒʌŋkʃən','''dʒʌŋkʃn','[n] 交叉点， 汇合处； 连接， 接合','the junction of Abbot Road and Mill Street  阿伯特路与米尔街的交叉口'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3022','electrolysis','ɪ,lɛk''trɑləsɪs','ɪˌlek''trɑːləsɪs','[n] 电解作用； 电解术','Instead, he says, the solution to large-scale hydrogen production lies in using renewable electricity to extract hydrogen from water via electrolysis.  相反他认为大规模生产氢的解决方案在于使用可更新的电通过电解方式从水中提取氢。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3023','bandanna','bæn''dænə','bæn''dænə','[n] 色彩鲜艳的围巾',''),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3024','instinct','''ɪnstɪŋkt','''ɪnstɪŋkt','[n] 本能， 直觉； 生性， 天性','Her instinct told her that something was wrong.  直觉告诉她有些不对劲。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3025','gourmet','''ɡʊrme','''gurmeɪ','[adj] 美味的; [n] 美食家','a gourmet cook  美食厨师'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3026','reputation',',rɛpju''teʃən','ˌrepju''teɪʃn','[n] 名声， 声望， 名誉','Alice Munro has a reputation for being a very depressing writer.  艾丽斯•门罗有文风抑郁的名声。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3027','spike','spaɪk','spaɪk','[n] 长钉， 大钉； 猛增， 急升',''),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3028','shrub','ʃrʌb','ʃrʌb','[n] 灌木','...flowering shrubs.  …开花的灌木。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3029','presentation',',prizɛn''teʃən','ˌpriːzen''teɪʃn','[n] 提供， 显示； 介绍， 陈述； 赠送； 表演','We will begin a series of presentations to help the public fully understand our system.  我们将进行一系列的说明，帮助公众充分了解我们的制度。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3030','genesis','''dʒɛnəsɪs','''dʒenəsɪs','[n] 起源， 开端','The project had its genesis two years earlier.  该项目是两年前开始的。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3031','subliminal',',sʌb''lɪmɪnl','ˌsʌb''lɪmɪnl','[adj] 下意识的， 潜意识的','a subliminal message  潜在的含义'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3032','engrave','ɪn''ɡrev','ɪn''greɪv','[vt] 雕刻； 铭刻','Your wedding ring can be engraved with a personal inscription at no extra cost.  你的结婚戒指可以刻上个人题字不另收费。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3033','tavern','''tævɚn','''tævərn','[n] 小旅馆， 客栈； 小酒店','Murphy’s Tavern  墨菲酒馆'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3034','glimmer','''ɡlɪmɚ','''glɪmər','[vi] 发微光； 隐约出现; [n] 闪烁的微光；隐约的迹象；一丝，一线','a weak glimmering light  微弱的闪光'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3035','awkward','''ɔkwɚd','''ɔːkwərd','[adj] 别扭的； 笨拙的； 难处理的， 棘手的； 难操纵的','Amy made an awkward gesture with her hands.  艾米用双手做了一个笨拙的手势。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3036','adhesive','əd''hisɪv','əd''hiːsɪv','[adj] 带黏性的; [n] 胶合剂','...adhesive tape.  …胶布。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3037','monumental',',mɑnju''mɛntl','ˌmɑːnju''mentl','[adj] 纪念碑的； 不朽的','a monumental arch  纪念拱门'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3038','ruin','''ruɪn','''ruːɪn','[vt] 破坏，毁灭；使破产; [n] 毁灭，毁坏；','Jefferson was ruined by the lawsuit.  杰弗逊因为那场官司倾家荡产。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3039','spill','spɪl','spɪl','[v] 溢出，溅出；蜂拥而出; [n] 溢出， 泄漏','Katie almost spilled her milk.  凯蒂差点把牛奶洒出来。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3040','celebrate','sɛləˌbret','''selɪbreɪt','[v] 赞美； 庆祝','It’s Dad’s birthday and we’re going out for a meal to celebrate.  今天是爸爸的生日，我们打算出去吃饭庆祝一下。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3041','cradle','''kredl','''kreɪdl','[n] 摇篮； 发源地','She rocked the cradle to quieten the child.  她摇动摇篮，让宝宝安静下来。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3042','abut','ə''bʌt','ə''bʌt','[v] 邻接， 毗邻','The castles abut a natural forest.  与城堡毗邻的是一片天然森林。'),
