('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3494','jar','dʒɑr','dʒɑːr','[v] 震动；冲突，抵触；感到不快; [n] 坛子； 广口瓶','His enthusiasm jarred.  他的热情令人厌烦。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3495','poverty','''pɑvɚti','''pɑːvərti','[n] 贫穷， 贫困','Millions of elderly people live in poverty .  数百万老年人生活在贫困之中。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3496','repertoire','''rɛpɚ''twɑr','''repərtwɑːr','[n] 常备剧目， 保留剧目； 可表演节目； 全部才能','the behavioural repertoire of infants  婴幼儿的行为能力'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3497','resort','rɪ''zɔrt','rɪ''zɔːrt','[vi] 求助; [n] 度假胜地； 手段','His punishing work schedule had made him resort to drugs.  他那累人的工作日程已经使他不得不求助于毒品了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3498','dwindle','''dwɪndl','''dwɪndl','[v] 减少； 缩小','The elephant population is dwindling.  大象的数量在减少。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3499','lightning','''laɪtnɪŋ','''laɪtnɪŋ','[adj] 闪电般的， 快速的; [n] 闪电','a lightning attack  闪电式突袭'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3500','jaw','dʒɔ','dʒɔː','[n] 颌，颚；','a broken jaw  碎裂的颌骨'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3501','reef','rif','riːf','[n] 礁， 暗礁','a proposal to protect several miles of thousand-year-old coral reef  保护绵延数英里的千年古珊瑚礁的提案'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3502','margin','''mɑrdʒən','''mɑːrdʒən','[n] 边缘； 页边空白； 差数， 差额； 余地， 余裕','Someone had scribbled a note in the margin .  有人在页边写了条批注。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3503','nail','nel','neɪl','[n] 指甲，爪；钉; [vt] 将…钉牢， 钉住','The key was hanging on a nail by the door.  钥匙挂在门边的一颗钉子上。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3504','tarnish','''tɑrnɪʃ','''tɑːrnɪʃ','[v] 失去光泽；玷污，败坏; [n] 污点； 瑕疵','His regime was tarnished by human rights abuses.  他的政权因践踏人权而形象受损。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3505','sunlit','''sʌnlɪt','''sʌnlɪt','[adj] 阳光照射的','a sunlit garden  阳光灿烂的花园'),
