('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3507','mount','maʊnt','maunt','[v] 增加；登上，攀登；骑上，乘上；发起，组织，开展; [n] 山， 山峰； 支架， 底座','The National Gallery mounted an exhibition of Danish painting.  国家美术馆举办了丹麦画展。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3508','coexist',',koɪɡ''zɪst','ˌkouɪg''zɪst','[vi] 共存','But I think both can coexist.  但是我认为两者可以共存。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3509','acquiesce',',ækwi''es','ˌækwi''es','[vi] 默许， 默认','Steve seemed to acquiesce in the decision.  斯蒂夫看样子默许了这个决定。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3510','pathetic','pə''θɛtɪk','pə''θetɪk','[adj] 可怜的， 引起怜悯的， 令人怜惜的','The child looked a pathetic sight.  那个孩子看上去很可怜。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3511','turkey','''tɝki','''tɜːrki','[n] 火鸡； 失败','roast turkey  烤火鸡'),
