('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3548','dilemma','dəˈlɛmə, daɪ-','dɪ''lemə','[n] 困境， 进退两难的局面','a moral dilemma  道德上进退两难的窘境'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3549','rub','rʌb','rʌb','[n&v] 擦， 摩擦','You’ll have to rub harder if you want to get it clean.  如果你想把它弄干净，就得更使劲地擦。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3550','through','θru','θruː','[adv] 从头到尾，自始至终；直达，径直；彻底，完全; [adj] 完成的， 结束的； 直达的， 直通的; [prep] 穿过，通过；从头到尾，自始至终；经由，以；因为，由于','She smiled at him as he walked through the door.  他从门口进来时，她朝他笑了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3551','rug','rʌɡ','rʌg','[n] 地毯； 围毯','A Persian rug covered the hardwood floors.  一张波斯小地毯铺在了那硬木地板上。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3552','hieroglyph','''haɪərəɡlɪf','''haɪərəglɪf','[n] 象形文字， 象形符号','A picture representing a word or idea; a hieroglyph.  象形文字代表一个字或意义的图画；'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3553','towering','''taʊərɪŋ','''tauərɪŋ','[adj] 高耸的； 杰出的','great towering cliffs  雄伟高耸的峭壁'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3554','occasional','ə''keʒənl','ə''keɪʒənl','[adj] 偶然的， 不经常的； 临时的','He made occasional visits to London.  他有时候会去伦敦。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3555','enact','ɪ''nækt','ɪ''nækt','[v] 制定法律， 颁布； 扮演','a drama enacted on a darkened stage  在灯光暗淡的舞台上演的戏剧'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3556','deviant','''divɪənt','''diːviənt','[adj] 不正常的，越出常规的; [n] 不正常的人','deviant behaviour  变态的行为'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3557','pharaoh','','''ferou','[n] 法老','They were not quasi-divine overmen like pharaoh or minos or the monarchs of mesopotamia.  他们并不像法老、弥诺斯或美索不达米亚君主那样类似上帝的超人。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3558','scrutinize','''skrutənaɪz','''skruːtənaɪz','[v] 仔细检查， 细察','He scrutinized the document.  他细阅了这份文件。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3559','realtor','','''riːəltər','[n] 房地产经纪人','In england they call a realtor a land agent .  在英国他们叫作房地产经纪人。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3560','debate','dɪ''bet','dɪ''beɪt','[v&n] 辩论； 讨论， 争论','the gun-control debate in the US  美国有关控制枪支的争论'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3561','spacecraft','''speskræft','''speɪskræft','[n] 航天器， 宇宙飞船','...the world''s largest and most expensive unmanned spacecraft.  …世界上最大、最贵的无人航天器。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3562','extinguish','ɪk''stɪŋɡwɪʃ','ɪk''stɪŋgwɪʃ','[vt] 熄灭， 扑灭； 消灭， 毁灭， 使破灭','Please extinguish all cigarettes.  请把香烟都熄灭了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3563','vulnerable','''vʌlnərəbl','''vʌlnərəbl','[adj] 易受攻击的， 易受伤的','He took advantage of me when I was at my most vulnerable.  他在我最脆弱的时候利用了我。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3564','preach','pritʃ','priːtʃ','[v] 布道， 讲道； 竭力鼓吹， 宣讲， 宣传； 说教','He traveled the southern states, preaching the gospel .  他游历南方各州宣讲福音。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3565','fibrous','''faɪbrəs','''faɪbrəs','[adj] 含纤维的； 纤维状的','The coconut has a fibrous outer covering.  椰子有一个纤维质的外壳。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3566','recollection',',rɛkə''lɛkʃən','ˌrekə''lekʃn','[n] 记忆力； 回忆， 记忆； 回想起来的事','My earliest recollections are of my mother bending over my cot.  我最早的记忆是母亲俯身站在我的小床前。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3567','subjugate','''sʌbdʒuɡet','''sʌbdʒugeɪt','[vt] 征服， 制伏， 使服从','The native population was subjugated and exploited.  土著人被征服，并遭受剥削。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3568','donate','''donet','''douneɪt','[vt] 捐赠； 赠送','people who volunteer to donate blood  自愿献血者'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3569','deplete','dɪ''plit','dɪ''pliːt','[vt] 使枯竭， 耗尽','...substances that deplete the ozone layer.  …消耗臭氧层的物质。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3570','bonanza','bə''nænzə','bə''nænzə','[n] 富矿带； 带来好运的事； 兴盛， 繁荣','The expected sales bonanza hadn''t materialized.  预期的销售大涨并未成为现实。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3571','statistic','stə''tɪstɪk','stə''tɪstɪk','[n] 统计数字，统计资料；','The statistic comes from a study recently conducted by the British government.  这项统计数据来自英国政府最近进行的一项研究。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3572','nicotine','''nɪkətɪn','''nɪkətiːn','[n] 尼古丁','Nicotine produces a feeling of well-being in the smoker.  尼古丁能让吸烟者产生一种愉悦的感觉。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3573','taboo','tə''bu','tə''buː','[adj] 忌讳的; [n] 禁忌，忌讳；禁止，避讳','Rape is a taboo subject .  强奸是忌讳的话题。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3574','mold','mold','mould','[n] 霉菌；模型; [vt] 塑造','Because of its flexibility, we can mold software into any form to do almost anything.  由于灵活性，我们可以将软件塑造成任何形式从而处理几乎所有的问题。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3575','bold','bold','bould','[adj] 大胆的； 冒失的； 粗体的； 醒目的','In a surprisingly bold move , he is threatening court action against the company.  他出人意料地做出一个大胆举动，威胁要起诉这家公司。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3576','significant','sɪɡ''nɪfɪkənt','sɪg''nɪfɪkənt','[adj] 有重大意义的， 重要的， 显著的； 意味深长的','His most significant political achievement was the abolition of the death penalty.  他政治上最重大的成就是废除了死刑。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3577','tentacle','''tɛntəkl','''tentəkl','[n] 触角， 触须， 触手','Free speech is being gradually eroded year after year by new tentacles of government control.  言论自由正被政府控制的新触角逐渐侵蚀。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3578','overlap','''ovəlæp','əʊvə''læp','[v] 交叠， 部分重叠; [n] 重叠； 重叠的部分','When the bag is folded, the bottom overlaps one side.  把包折叠起来时，其底部与一边就重合了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3579','volunteer',',vɑlən''tɪr','ˌvɑːlən''tɪr','[v] 自愿做; [adj] 志愿的， 义务的; [n] 志愿者；志愿军','I volunteered my services as a driver.  我主动提出来当司机。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3580','senate','''sɛnət','''senət','[n] 参议院； 上院','The Senate approved the bill.  参议院批准了这项议案。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3581','assassinate','ə''sæsn''et','ə''sæsəneɪt','[vt] 暗杀， 行刺； 诋毁','a plot to assassinate the President  刺杀总统的阴谋'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3582','crow','kro','krou','[v] 啼叫， 打鸣； 得意洋洋; [n] 乌鸦','Ben rushed to his father, crowing with pleasure.  本欢叫着跑向他爸爸。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3583','bolt','bolt','boult','[v] 逃跑；闩上; [n] 插销， 门闩； 闪电','He reminded her that he would have to lock and bolt the kitchen door after her.  他提醒她，他得在她离开后锁上厨房的门并插上门闩。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3584','congressional','kən''ɡrɛʃənl','kən''greʃənl','[adj] 立法机构的； 代表大会的； 国会的','The president explained his plans to congressional leaders.  总统向国会领导人说明了他的计划。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3585','boon','bʊn','buːn','[n] 恩惠， 恩赐； 益处','The bus service is a real boon to people in the village.  公共汽车服务对村里的人来说是一大便利之处。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3586','novelty','''nɑvlti','''nɑːvlti','[n] 新奇， 新颖； 新奇的事物','Many toys have no attraction beyond their novelty value.  许多玩具除了有些新奇感之外，别无吸引力。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3587','boom','buːm','buːm','[vi] 迅速发展，激增；发出低沉有力的声音; [n] 激增， 繁荣； 繁荣昌盛期','Business was booming , and money wasn’t a problem.  生意非常兴隆，钱已不是问题。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3588','abolish','ə''bɑlɪʃ','ə''bɑːlɪʃ','[vt] 废止， 废除','Slavery was abolished in the US in the 19th century.  美国于19世纪废除了奴隶制。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3589','absence','''æbsns','''æbsəns','[n] 缺席； 缺乏','In the absence of any evidence, the police had to let Myers go.  警察没有证据，只好把迈尔斯放了。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3590','attract','ə''trækt','ə''trækt','[vt] 吸引','I’m not usually attracted to blondes.  我一般不喜欢金发女子。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3591','critique','krɪ''tik','krɪ''tiːk','[n] 批评，评论; [vt] 写评论','She had brought a book, a feminist critique of Victorian lady novelists.  她带来了一本书，一本从女权主义角度对维多利亚时期女小说家进行的评论。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3592','cautious','''kɔʃəs','''kɔːʃəs','[adj] 小心的， 谨慎的','a cautious driver  一位谨慎的司机'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3593','recession','rɪ''sɛʃən','rɪ''seʃn','[n] 衰退， 衰退时期， 萧条时期； 撤回， 退回','the economic recession of the early 1980s  20世纪80年代初的经济衰退'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3594','situated','''sɪtʃuetɪd','''sɪtʃueɪtɪd','[adj] 坐落在…的； 处于…境地的','His hotel is situated in one of the loveliest places on the Loire.  他的旅馆坐落在卢瓦尔的一个最优美的地方。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3595','malicious','mə''lɪʃəs','mə''lɪʃəs','[adj] 怀有恶意的， 恶毒的','a malicious girl  恶毒的女孩'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3596','vigilance','''vɪdʒələns','''vɪdʒɪləns','[n] 警戒， 警惕','the need for increased police vigilance  警方加强警戒的必要性'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3597','ally','''ælaɪ','''ælaɪ','[v] 结盟; [n] 同盟国； 结盟者， 支持者','He will have no choice but to ally himself with the new movement.  他将别无选择，只能与这个新运动结盟。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3598','concentric','kən''sɛntrɪk','kən''sentrɪk','[adj] 同心的','concentric circles  同心圆'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3599','mantle','''mæntl','''mæntl','[n] 覆盖物； 披风， 斗篷； 纱罩； 【地】地幔','The parks and squares looked grim under a mantle of soot and ash.  在一层烟尘的笼罩下，这些公园和广场显得阴沉沉的。 '),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3600','outrageous','aʊt''redʒəs','aut''reɪdʒəs','[adj] 残暴的； 骇人的； 反常的， 过度的','outrageous prices  骇人的价格'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3601','abbreviate','ə''brivɪ''et','ə''briːvieɪt','[vt] 缩略， 缩写','The creators of the original X-Men abbreviated the title of its sequel to simply X2.  第1部《X战警》的创作者们把其续集的片名缩写成简单的《X2》。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3602','lavish','''lævɪʃ','''lævɪʃ','[adj] 大方的， 慷慨的； 大量的； 浪费的; [vt] 慷慨给予，滥用；浪费，挥霍','a royal palace on a lavish scale  庞大的皇宫'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3603','substance','''sʌbstəns','''sʌbstəns','[n] 物质； 主旨， 实质； 根据； 重要性','The leaves were covered with a strange sticky substance.  树叶上覆着一层黏糊糊的怪东西。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3604','varnish','''vɑrnɪʃ','''vɑːrnɪʃ','[vt] 上清漆; [n] 清漆','Varnish the table with two or three coats of water-based varnish.  给桌子涂上2到3层水性清漆。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3605','tribal','''traɪbl','''traɪbl','[adj] 部落的， 宗族的； 种族的','a tribal dance  部落舞蹈'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3606','bond','bɑnd','bɑːnd','[v] 黏合， 结合; [n] 联结，黏结；债券；黏合剂；契约，合同','It takes less than ten minutes for the two surfaces to bond.  用不了十分钟两个表面就会黏合起来。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3607','momentum','mo''mɛntəm','mou''mentəm','[n] 动量； 动力， 冲力； 势头','incentives to maintain the momentum of European integration  保持欧洲一体化发展势头的激励措施'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3608','target','''tɑrɡɪt','''tɑːrgɪt','[n] 目标，对象；靶子; [vt] 把…作为目标','There is no target date for completion of the new project.  这个新的项目何时完工没有预定日期。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3609','discourse','''dɪskɔrs','''dɪskɔːs; -''kɔːs','[vi] 讲述， 论述; [n] 演讲； 论文； 话语','a study of spoken discourse  口语语篇研究'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3610','obstruct','əb''strʌkt','əb''strʌkt','[vt] 妨碍， 阻挠； 阻塞','A small aircraft was obstructing the runway.  一架小型飞机堵住了跑道。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3611','grind','ɡraɪnd','graɪnd','[v] 打磨；磨，碾; [n] 磨碎， 碾碎； 苦差事','a stone for grinding knives and scissors  磨刀剪的石头'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3612','bony','''boni','''bouni','[adj] 瘦骨嶙峋的； 似骨的； 多骨的','She had a bony intelligent face.  她的脸很瘦，看来很聪明。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3613','labyrinth','''læbərɪnθ','''læbərɪnθ','[n] 迷宫； 错综复杂的事件','...the labyrinth of corridors.  …迷宫般的走廊。'),
('TOEFL_3','TOEFL_3_3614','aquatic','ə''kwætɪk','ə''kwætɪk','[adj] 水生的； 水上的','an aquatic plant  水生植物'),
