('SAT_2','SAT_2_768','erratic','ɪ''rætɪk','ɪ''rætɪk','[adj] 不稳定的；古怪的; [n] 漂泊无定的人；古怪的人','His breathing was becoming erratic.  他的呼吸越来越不均匀。'),
('SAT_2','SAT_2_769','reck','rek','rek','[vt] 顾虑；和…相干; [vi] 介意；有关系; [n] (Reck)人名；(英、德、匈、波)雷克','to reck nought'),
('SAT_2','SAT_2_770','instruct','ɪn''strʌkt','ɪn''strʌkt','[v] 指导；通知；命令；教授','Eva went straight to the hotel, as instructed (= as she had been told ).  伊娃按照指示径直去了宾馆。'),
('SAT_2','SAT_2_771','substantiate','səb''stænʃɪet','səb''stænʃɪeɪt','[v] 证实；使实体化','Katzen offered little evidence to substantiate his claims .  卡曾拿不出什么证据来证明他的说法。'),
('SAT_2','SAT_2_772','centurion','sɛn''tʃʊrɪən','sen''tjʊərɪən','[n] 百夫长；百人队队长','And as they bound him with thongs, Paul said unto the centurion that stood by, Is it lawful for you to scourge a man that is a Roman, and uncondemned?  刚用皮条捆上，保罗对旁边站着的百夫长说，人是罗马人，又没有定罪，你们就鞭打他，有这个例吗。'),
