('SAT_2','SAT_2_3474','evidence','''ɛvɪdəns','''evɪd(ə)ns','[n] 证据，证明；迹象；明显; [v] 证明','Murrow’s evidence was enough to convict Hayes of murder.  默罗的证词足以证明海斯犯了谋杀罪。'),
('SAT_2','SAT_2_3475','stimulus','''stɪmjələs','''stɪmjʊləs','[n] 刺激；激励；刺激物','Tax cuts provided the stimulus which the slow economy needed.  减税为不景气的经济带来了其所需的刺激。'),
('SAT_2','SAT_2_3476','credo','''krido','''kriːdəʊ; ''kreɪ-','[n] 信条，教义','American Express is emphasizing its ‘the customer is first’ credo.  美国运通公司强调其“客户至上”的信条。'),
('SAT_2','SAT_2_3477','blaze','blez','bleɪz','[v] 在树皮上刻路标；公开宣布; [n] 火焰，烈火；光辉；情感爆发','an innovative young company that has blazed a trail for others to follow  一家勇于创新的年轻公司，开辟了一条可供效法的新路径'),
